1
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:24,690
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:58,160 --> 00:03:00,380
I considered you more than a brother...

3
00:03:01,820 --> 00:03:04,440
...entrusted my son to you.

4
00:03:06,340 --> 00:03:11,560
However, an ambush took you apart
from me.

5
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:14,960
Ahmet...

6
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:19,040
I swear on Ahmet that...

7
00:03:19,820 --> 00:03:22,420
...I will establish justice.

8
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:36,580
I stopped because you told me to do so.

9
00:03:37,900 --> 00:03:39,700
I will set their tents on fire.

10
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:43,900
I will destroy the castles
they conquered.

11
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:48,860
Atabey...

12
00:03:50,540 --> 00:03:52,720
...was in the same position as you
for me.

13
00:03:54,300 --> 00:03:57,340
This is now a blood case, father.

14
00:03:58,440 --> 00:04:00,380
Don't worry, son.

15
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:07,080
Firstly, we will weaken them with policiy.

16
00:04:08,220 --> 00:04:10,100
If they don't give Turgut to us...

17
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:16,480
...we'll perform more than
what we talk about.

18
00:04:56,180 --> 00:04:58,540
I have known Osman for years.

19
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:01,300
He will never leave things to chance.

20
00:05:02,340 --> 00:05:05,460
So dig out Ahmet's body right now.

21
00:05:09,300 --> 00:05:11,320
We'll save him from Osman.

22
00:05:12,060 --> 00:05:17,800
Also, we'll take him to Nikea and
hold a funeral as he deserves.

23
00:05:18,050 --> 00:05:20,300
Are you sure Osman will come?

24
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:23,600
We should never let our guards down.

25
00:05:24,660 --> 00:05:26,820
Darkness is always with you.

26
00:05:32,280 --> 00:05:35,560
If he comes, finish him.

27
00:05:39,740 --> 00:05:40,580
Come on.

28
00:06:00,940 --> 00:06:01,780
My Bey!

29
00:06:08,140 --> 00:06:09,840
- My Bey!
- Tell me, Baysungur.

30
00:06:09,840 --> 00:06:13,200
As you command, I have been following them
since they left the tents.

31
00:06:13,200 --> 00:06:14,770
They buried Ahmet.

32
00:06:20,780 --> 00:06:21,500
My Bey!

33
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:23,500
Excuse me...

34
00:06:24,380 --> 00:06:26,450
We are riding horses after a dead man.

35
00:06:28,100 --> 00:06:29,780
What do you expect to find?

36
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:32,920
The dead speaks...

37
00:06:35,540 --> 00:06:37,360
...when the living stays silent.

38
00:06:41,940 --> 00:06:43,340
Come on Alps!

39
00:07:20,340 --> 00:07:22,280
Hurry up!
Hustle your bustle!

40
00:07:30,780 --> 00:07:33,140
I was suspicious until now.

41
00:07:34,620 --> 00:07:36,440
But now, I am sure.

42
00:07:37,700 --> 00:07:40,870
They are afraid of that
even the dead might tell something.

43
00:07:42,440 --> 00:07:44,820
My curiosity has been satisfied, my Bey.

44
00:07:53,780 --> 00:07:56,940
Atabey dies
Cobanoglu buries.

45
00:07:57,080 --> 00:07:59,900
Byzantine digs out.

46
00:08:00,840 --> 00:08:03,300
When it is about the future of Turks...

47
00:08:04,100 --> 00:08:06,600
...all the devils come together!

48
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:21,940
Let's go.

49
00:08:43,679 --> 00:08:45,600
Come on Alps.

50
00:08:48,480 --> 00:08:49,720
My Bey!

51
00:09:01,680 --> 00:09:02,560
Duck!

52
00:09:20,040 --> 00:09:21,220
Attack!

53
00:09:27,380 --> 00:09:28,360
Baysungur!

54
00:09:29,520 --> 00:09:31,130
Since Atabey...

55
00:09:32,710 --> 00:09:35,250
...we haven't been able to fight
back to back.

56
00:09:35,250 --> 00:09:36,680
You missed me, right?

57
00:09:37,520 --> 00:09:39,120
O Allah!

58
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:07,180
Soldier!

59
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:09,460
Our duty is to take this body away!

60
00:10:09,460 --> 00:10:11,120
Come on!
Take it!

61
00:10:45,300 --> 00:10:46,540
Come to me.

62
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:22,020
There must a sign.

63
00:11:22,780 --> 00:11:25,300
As those dogs want to hide him
from us...T

64
00:11:27,040 --> 00:11:28,880
...there must definitely be a sign.

65
00:11:31,620 --> 00:11:32,980
Take him...

66
00:11:33,340 --> 00:11:34,660
...to the tents.

67
00:11:35,300 --> 00:11:36,560
Come on!

68
00:11:43,140 --> 00:11:46,660
Cobanoglu Ali and Osman will
fall out for each other.

69
00:11:46,820 --> 00:11:48,280
This is inevitable.

70
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:51,960
Osman's blood is enough for all of us,
Romanos.

71
00:11:52,660 --> 00:11:54,300
This revenge is all of ours.

72
00:11:56,420 --> 00:11:58,260
They will splinter.

73
00:11:58,560 --> 00:12:00,860
We won't stop
in the opposite case!

74
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:06,220
Our moves will continue until
Osman is removed.

75
00:12:07,080 --> 00:12:09,240
So let your soldiers stay tight.

76
00:12:09,820 --> 00:12:11,780
I will need them.

77
00:12:13,640 --> 00:12:14,920
I'll come back again.

78
00:12:46,820 --> 00:12:47,860
Cebe.

79
00:12:49,620 --> 00:12:52,390
What is the reason of this
disrespect of your soldiers'?

80
00:12:52,400 --> 00:12:57,380
If you try to leave here
before Cebe finishes his words...

81
00:12:59,640 --> 00:13:06,720
...the cold Mongol sword might
cut your neck.

82
00:13:08,040 --> 00:13:10,400
We talked what we had to talk.

83
00:13:13,900 --> 00:13:15,540
We set our plan.

84
00:13:16,780 --> 00:13:18,700
You took your share of gold.

85
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:22,720
What do you want me more?

86
00:13:23,260 --> 00:13:24,520
Osman.

87
00:13:26,540 --> 00:13:30,040
Defeating him in his tents is impossible.

88
00:13:31,220 --> 00:13:33,060
He will come to me.

89
00:13:33,200 --> 00:13:34,980
Osman is a wise man.

90
00:13:36,240 --> 00:13:38,240
We can't drag him here easily.

91
00:13:38,760 --> 00:13:41,100
Remember that we are playing
against a devil.

92
00:13:49,260 --> 00:13:50,640
The devil...

93
00:13:57,160 --> 00:13:58,960
...is me, Romanos.

94
00:14:00,620 --> 00:14:01,740
What is your plan?

95
00:14:11,760 --> 00:14:13,980
We'll gain trust first.

96
00:14:27,300 --> 00:14:29,300
The time has come.

97
00:14:30,180 --> 00:14:31,260
Aktemur.

98
00:14:31,720 --> 00:14:32,490
My Bey.

99
00:14:33,400 --> 00:14:35,340
Sit there, will you?

100
00:14:38,880 --> 00:14:41,120
Sit on your father Gunduz Bey's place.

101
00:14:41,540 --> 00:14:42,480
Come on.

102
00:14:59,980 --> 00:15:03,720
Son, you will take care
of your father's heritage.

103
00:15:04,680 --> 00:15:08,020
His post is now yours.

104
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:10,960
My Bey...

105
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:16,100
...my duty is to be worthy of
my martyred father and you.

106
00:15:16,540 --> 00:15:19,260
Our hearts beat the same.
Our target is the same.

107
00:15:19,540 --> 00:15:20,720
Eyvallah
(thank you).

108
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:25,120
Hay Masha Allah (praise be!)

109
00:15:26,080 --> 00:15:28,680
You will do well in your post, Aktemur.

110
00:15:30,140 --> 00:15:33,280
Now that you have the post, the command...

111
00:15:33,720 --> 00:15:37,800
...we will call you Aktemur Bey
from now on.

112
00:15:45,350 --> 00:15:46,900
Masha Allah (praise be!)

113
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:50,890
Masha Allah.

114
00:15:50,930 --> 00:15:52,260
Can I come in, my Bey?

115
00:15:53,900 --> 00:15:55,070
Come!

116
00:16:00,650 --> 00:16:01,660
My Bey!

117
00:16:02,840 --> 00:16:05,390
Other tribe Beys want to see you.

118
00:16:10,400 --> 00:16:13,640
So you are not the ones who
are in need.

119
00:16:16,670 --> 00:16:17,870
Let them come.

120
00:16:42,070 --> 00:16:43,910
Do you see what's happening, Selvi?

121
00:16:44,070 --> 00:16:46,290
Do you see the trouble
Osman led us?

122
00:16:46,820 --> 00:16:49,630
He is not even aware of his mistakes
because of his pride!

123
00:16:49,630 --> 00:16:53,350
Osman leads not only himself but also us
to the cliff!

124
00:16:53,520 --> 00:16:56,380
Listen to me.
Do not turn your back to Osman Bey again.

125
00:16:56,440 --> 00:17:00,560
Just calm down.
Osman Bey must have a plan.

126
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:03,849
Don't you trust your Bey
as much as you trust Osman Bey?

127
00:17:04,490 --> 00:17:06,760
Do you hear what you say?

128
00:17:06,950 --> 00:17:08,898
What are you talking about, Barkin?!

129
00:17:08,990 --> 00:17:12,790
I always trust you!
Don't you see that I stand with you?

130
00:17:13,970 --> 00:17:17,000
Then do not question my words.

131
00:17:18,348 --> 00:17:20,670
Stand with your Bey.

132
00:17:21,300 --> 00:17:22,700
I stand with you.

133
00:17:23,210 --> 00:17:27,040
But it is my duty to tell the truth
to my Bey, to my lover.

134
00:17:27,140 --> 00:17:28,830
I haven't done anything wrong!

135
00:17:29,920 --> 00:17:31,940
I do not do it for myself.

136
00:17:32,940 --> 00:17:37,440
I'm doing what I'm doing in order to protect
you and my tribe, my father's memento!

137
00:17:38,820 --> 00:17:44,080
Do what you need to do.
Stand with your Bey.

138
00:17:45,720 --> 00:17:52,260
Now choose one.
Kizilbeyogullari tribe or Kayi tribe?

139
00:17:55,430 --> 00:18:00,970
Osman is leading not only us, but also
all the Turkmen tribes to trouble!

140
00:18:03,720 --> 00:18:09,850
Tell me Hatun! Do you choose
Kizilbeyogullari tribe or Kayi tribe?

141
00:18:12,200 --> 00:18:16,130
If you want to care your tribe
like me...

142
00:18:17,340 --> 00:18:22,460
...you will stay in Kayi tribe and
provide me with information.

143
00:18:48,530 --> 00:18:50,250
Welcome.

144
00:18:50,990 --> 00:18:52,410
Have a seat.

145
00:19:02,670 --> 00:19:06,380
Bey's tent is a council for consultation.

146
00:19:07,350 --> 00:19:13,140
You express your opinions here.

147
00:19:14,350 --> 00:19:15,410
Obviously...

148
00:19:16,640 --> 00:19:18,910
...there is something that worries you.

149
00:19:20,030 --> 00:19:21,530
Tell me.
I am listening.

150
00:19:21,830 --> 00:19:27,200
Osman Bey, the situation that we contrasted
with Cobanoglu Ali Bey isn't good at all.

151
00:19:28,720 --> 00:19:30,220
You are right.

152
00:19:30,990 --> 00:19:32,910
Not good at all.

153
00:19:33,220 --> 00:19:38,010
He came to stand with us,
but now he stands against us.

154
00:19:41,810 --> 00:19:45,970
My Bey!
Ali Bey is very close to Sultan Alaeddin.

155
00:19:47,210 --> 00:19:51,840
If this case goes to Sultan Alaeddin,
we will be in a great trouble, my Bey.

156
00:19:56,800 --> 00:20:01,880
Should we have been afraid,
stepped back and delivered Turgut Bey?

157
00:20:05,720 --> 00:20:09,580
No.
The court will make the decision.

158
00:20:10,440 --> 00:20:14,950
No matter who you are contrasted with,
even a Bey, or a Sultan...

159
00:20:16,120 --> 00:20:18,050
...there is only one truth.

160
00:20:19,330 --> 00:20:22,050
The right will not change
when there is an obstacle.

161
00:20:23,540 --> 00:20:25,460
I even doubt what I saw.

162
00:20:26,630 --> 00:20:28,690
We cannot judge by what we have heard.

163
00:20:29,450 --> 00:20:33,460
You are talking nice and easy, Konur Bey,
but the infidels are building up an army.

164
00:20:33,930 --> 00:20:38,010
We had a power against them with Ali Bey.
But now, we don't have Ali Bey.

165
00:20:40,850 --> 00:20:45,480
Let the court serve the justice.

166
00:20:46,430 --> 00:20:51,280
Then, Ali Bey will return from his
mistake and support us again.

167
00:20:52,170 --> 00:20:54,560
Don't worry, aghas.

168
00:20:55,770 --> 00:20:58,150
You speak truly.

169
00:20:58,660 --> 00:21:00,960
We lost a great ally.

170
00:21:01,970 --> 00:21:03,890
Who will benefit from this?

171
00:21:04,290 --> 00:21:06,600
Surely the enemy.

172
00:21:07,430 --> 00:21:11,510
But we'll talk about this at the council.

173
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:13,100
And make a decision.

174
00:21:13,480 --> 00:21:18,500
For that reason, you can go on now.

175
00:21:32,860 --> 00:21:35,660
It's Mongols who raided
the caravan.

176
00:21:37,080 --> 00:21:40,080
And then, Cebe came to us.

177
00:21:43,970 --> 00:21:45,820
We don't know who did this.

178
00:21:46,270 --> 00:21:48,170
But we know the time.

179
00:21:48,430 --> 00:21:52,810
So, keep your eyes on Cebe.

180
00:21:53,540 --> 00:21:55,170
As you order, my bey.

181
00:22:00,830 --> 00:22:03,570
They can plot all they want.

182
00:22:04,380 --> 00:22:07,220
They can try to divide us.

183
00:22:07,820 --> 00:22:09,870
But we don't have much time.

184
00:22:11,060 --> 00:22:15,950
We'll take Yenişehir before the
emperor comes to Yenişehir.

185
00:22:23,490 --> 00:22:25,070
Come on.

186
00:22:33,200 --> 00:22:35,000
Yenişehir.

187
00:22:58,430 --> 00:22:59,880
Allah is eternal.

188
00:23:00,210 --> 00:23:01,780
Allah is righteous.

189
00:23:01,990 --> 00:23:04,550
Allah is eternal.
Allah is righteous.

190
00:23:05,060 --> 00:23:08,030
Allah is eternal.
Allah is righteous.

191
00:23:08,340 --> 00:23:11,340
Allah is eternal.
Allah is righteous.

192
00:23:11,890 --> 00:23:14,260
Allah is eternal.
Allah is righteous.

193
00:23:14,870 --> 00:23:17,270
Allah is eternal.
Allah is righteous.

194
00:23:18,060 --> 00:23:19,410
Allah is eternal.

195
00:23:19,570 --> 00:23:23,240
The steel makes more
sound than you, smith.

196
00:23:24,180 --> 00:23:28,430
Which one of you is teaching
the other?

197
00:23:29,450 --> 00:23:31,320
Give me patience!

198
00:23:35,890 --> 00:23:40,240
Look at me, maybe I should strike
you instead.

199
00:23:40,870 --> 00:23:43,760
Let's see who makes more noise.

200
00:23:44,130 --> 00:23:45,630
Do you want it?

201
00:23:46,870 --> 00:23:49,390
Allah is eternal.
Allah is righteous.

202
00:23:49,780 --> 00:23:52,430
Allah is eternal.
Allah is righteous.

203
00:23:53,050 --> 00:23:54,400
Smith.

204
00:23:59,990 --> 00:24:02,610
Smith. Are you new?

205
00:24:03,980 --> 00:24:08,940
We wander around realms and
serve whoever needs it.

206
00:24:10,090 --> 00:24:12,140
Pack your things up.

207
00:24:12,840 --> 00:24:14,850
What is it, brother soldier?

208
00:24:15,470 --> 00:24:17,870
Why are you packing him up?

209
00:24:18,140 --> 00:24:20,600
Not just here, monk.

210
00:24:20,940 --> 00:24:26,610
All the smiths and armorers in Yenişehir
will be taken to the castle.

211
00:24:28,040 --> 00:24:31,640
We serve our lord. Sure.

212
00:24:32,490 --> 00:24:34,870
What will they do with so many?

213
00:24:35,110 --> 00:24:37,930
All the horseshoes will be repaired.

214
00:24:38,180 --> 00:24:39,820
Weapons too.

215
00:24:40,110 --> 00:24:43,540
Enough talking. Pack your
things and get to the castle.

216
00:24:43,730 --> 00:24:45,170
As you order.

217
00:24:45,670 --> 00:24:47,340
As you order.

218
00:24:58,690 --> 00:25:01,070
They are gathering a big army.

219
00:25:02,080 --> 00:25:04,540
For a big war.

220
00:25:05,290 --> 00:25:08,300
We need to inform Osman Bey
without wasting time.

221
00:25:10,570 --> 00:25:13,250
What are you waiting for?
Move.

222
00:25:21,760 --> 00:25:24,430
Allah is eternal.
Allah is righteous.

223
00:25:39,860 --> 00:25:42,470
Write everything I say.

224
00:25:45,260 --> 00:25:46,720
My sultan.

225
00:25:46,790 --> 00:25:49,440
I'll handle it!

226
00:25:54,370 --> 00:25:58,420
Osman went over his level.

227
00:26:00,180 --> 00:26:05,280
He is protecting the murderer of Atabey
Ahmet. He is breaking the order.

228
00:26:05,610 --> 00:26:09,170
He is proving his ill-intention.

229
00:26:10,660 --> 00:26:14,270
We await your orders to do
what's necessary.

230
00:26:15,600 --> 00:26:18,960
Choose the fastest horse and
take it to the sultan.

231
00:26:19,580 --> 00:26:20,910
As you order, my bey.

232
00:26:27,100 --> 00:26:30,280
Father. My wound is alright.

233
00:26:30,650 --> 00:26:32,490
I want to see Barkın Bey.

234
00:26:34,320 --> 00:26:36,560
For what?

235
00:26:36,780 --> 00:26:38,890
He is on Osman Bey's side.

236
00:26:39,560 --> 00:26:43,250
My atabey trusted him a lot.

237
00:26:43,360 --> 00:26:45,060
What will he do?

238
00:26:45,300 --> 00:26:50,370
If Osman Bey protects that murderer,
what can Osman Bey do?

239
00:26:51,030 --> 00:26:54,570
Isn't it better to make Osman Bey
lonelier?

240
00:26:55,700 --> 00:26:59,280
When Barkın Bey stands with us,
he'll be lonely.

241
00:27:00,500 --> 00:27:04,070
I'll do everything to avenge my atabey.

242
00:27:04,700 --> 00:27:10,510
Don't doubt it, Barkın Bey will
be our ally on this.

243
00:27:12,620 --> 00:27:14,920
Good then.

244
00:27:14,960 --> 00:27:18,820
Go but test Barkın Bey first.

245
00:27:19,430 --> 00:27:21,710
Then come and talk to me.

246
00:27:22,070 --> 00:27:26,120
Don't try to do something on
your own.

247
00:27:26,310 --> 00:27:27,700
As you order, father.

248
00:27:41,530 --> 00:27:43,850
-Şamil.
-My bey.

249
00:27:44,080 --> 00:27:47,570
Tell me. What's the situation?

250
00:27:47,970 --> 00:27:51,650
It's an arrow wound, my bey.
But the arrow was poisonous.

251
00:27:53,160 --> 00:27:56,240
It affects the mind.
It's not deadly.

252
00:27:56,600 --> 00:27:58,970
That's why he is still sleeping.

253
00:28:03,780 --> 00:28:08,050
So, they didn't shoot to kill
but to stop him.

254
00:28:09,290 --> 00:28:11,160
When will he wake up?

255
00:28:11,460 --> 00:28:16,420
It won't take long, inshallah.
He took the antidote.

256
00:28:16,620 --> 00:28:18,370
He'll be at his feet soon.

257
00:28:19,170 --> 00:28:21,410
Thank you.
Thank you.

258
00:28:23,620 --> 00:28:26,090
Kumral Abdal taught you well.

259
00:28:26,390 --> 00:28:27,770
Thank you, my bey.

260
00:29:22,770 --> 00:29:24,280
My bey.

261
00:29:25,030 --> 00:29:27,240
Cebe and his warriors are here.

262
00:29:27,420 --> 00:29:29,500
They have captured Mongols.

263
00:30:06,520 --> 00:30:08,190
Osman Bey...

264
00:30:09,890 --> 00:30:14,830
...a part of the rebels are here.

265
00:30:18,070 --> 00:30:20,280
These are just a few of them.

266
00:30:21,720 --> 00:30:25,790
Let them stay here.
I will go after the rest.

267
00:30:30,020 --> 00:30:32,640
Are they those who attacked Ali Bey's
caravan?

268
00:30:35,210 --> 00:30:39,940
They are rebels.
They are only trouble for the people.

269
00:30:41,110 --> 00:30:43,380
I don't know which caravan they looted.

270
00:30:44,300 --> 00:30:47,090
You wouldn't give them to me before making
them talk.

271
00:30:52,500 --> 00:30:54,060
Stay back.

272
00:30:57,400 --> 00:30:58,780
Osman Bey.

273
00:30:59,980 --> 00:31:01,740
Turahan.

274
00:31:02,690 --> 00:31:04,230
It is fine.

275
00:31:10,370 --> 00:31:13,240
Everyone screams about what they have
done but...

276
00:31:14,260 --> 00:31:16,670
...whisper what they couldn't.

277
00:31:20,030 --> 00:31:24,860
No matter what I did, I couldn't make them
say a word, Osman Bey.

278
00:31:26,140 --> 00:31:27,660
I hope you can.

279
00:31:28,980 --> 00:31:30,220
Turahan.

280
00:31:31,820 --> 00:31:33,660
Take them to the caged tent.

281
00:31:33,980 --> 00:31:35,660
As you order, my Bey.

282
00:31:50,280 --> 00:31:52,900
Now, if you will excuse me...

283
00:31:53,720 --> 00:31:55,730
...I will go after the rest of the rebels.

284
00:31:56,440 --> 00:31:59,260
If there is any news that will help me...

285
00:31:59,820 --> 00:32:02,100
...do not withhold it from me.

286
00:32:03,880 --> 00:32:09,900
What benefits you benefits me too, Osman
Bey.

287
00:32:12,540 --> 00:32:14,040
We have a common enemy.

288
00:33:20,420 --> 00:33:23,600
All of you will be caught by Osman.

289
00:33:29,200 --> 00:33:31,340
I will deliver you.

290
00:33:35,860 --> 00:33:39,160
When we are done with Osman...

291
00:33:44,060 --> 00:33:45,520
...all of you...

292
00:33:46,680 --> 00:33:50,820
....will be rewarded.

293
00:33:54,060 --> 00:33:56,000
Much gold...

294
00:33:58,380 --> 00:34:00,120
...many horses.

295
00:34:16,260 --> 00:34:18,340
They will interrogate you.

296
00:34:21,320 --> 00:34:23,239
They will make you bleed.

297
00:34:43,139 --> 00:34:45,340
You won't talk.

298
00:34:56,560 --> 00:34:59,700
They will starve you.

299
00:35:01,700 --> 00:35:03,060
I am sure of it.

300
00:35:04,300 --> 00:35:05,620
Drink!

301
00:35:06,400 --> 00:35:08,560
Drink as much as you can!

302
00:35:56,160 --> 00:35:59,800
Come on, hatuns! Bring the goods going
to Söğüt here!

303
00:36:12,480 --> 00:36:13,580
My Bey.

304
00:36:16,420 --> 00:36:20,100
You had doubts about Cebe.

305
00:36:20,580 --> 00:36:23,040
Has it increased or decreased?

306
00:36:23,140 --> 00:36:24,180
No.

307
00:36:24,980 --> 00:36:27,220
You can never trust them.

308
00:36:27,420 --> 00:36:31,220
He gives you his leash but watches
your hand.

309
00:36:31,720 --> 00:36:33,220
Thus...

310
00:36:34,480 --> 00:36:36,520
...we will be on alert.

311
00:36:37,280 --> 00:36:38,680
As you order.

312
00:36:43,500 --> 00:36:45,940
Our friend Cebe is setting the game.

313
00:36:47,080 --> 00:36:49,040
Osman is near his end.

314
00:36:49,700 --> 00:36:51,760
He can't escape anymore.

315
00:36:52,220 --> 00:36:56,080
I want to see Osman die more than
anything, Romanos.

316
00:36:56,640 --> 00:36:58,280
Know that I can't wait for it.

317
00:36:58,920 --> 00:37:00,860
We all want this.

318
00:37:01,380 --> 00:37:02,860
All of us.

319
00:37:03,620 --> 00:37:07,720
Besides, you being one of us helps our
games.

320
00:37:08,080 --> 00:37:09,860
Even Osman doesn't know but...

321
00:37:10,600 --> 00:37:13,400
...I am closer to him than his shadow.

322
00:37:14,380 --> 00:37:18,920
And I will never leave his side so as to
be the first one to see...

323
00:37:19,300 --> 00:37:21,080
...when he dies.

324
00:37:22,340 --> 00:37:23,960
This is exactly what we need.

325
00:37:25,080 --> 00:37:27,520
You should always stay with him so that...

326
00:37:28,040 --> 00:37:30,320
...we can be informed of everything
he does.

327
00:37:34,700 --> 00:37:38,300
If we are going to pull the ground under
Osman...

328
00:37:39,360 --> 00:37:42,300
...first, we must know which ground
he will step on.

329
00:37:43,340 --> 00:37:45,080
I am with him so that we do know.

330
00:37:46,400 --> 00:37:47,700
We will know.

331
00:37:49,100 --> 00:37:50,260
We will.

332
00:37:57,520 --> 00:38:01,820
By the ninety-nine names of Almighty Allah
who does when he says "Be"...

333
00:38:01,950 --> 00:38:08,310
...and fills our hearts with the light
of faith.

334
00:38:10,000 --> 00:38:12,140
In the name of Allah.

335
00:38:14,900 --> 00:38:17,080
Ali Bey turned his back on us.

336
00:38:18,220 --> 00:38:22,740
And emperor is sending a huge army to
attack us.

337
00:38:23,960 --> 00:38:26,200
Everything seems to be against us.

338
00:38:27,640 --> 00:38:28,680
But...

339
00:38:29,540 --> 00:38:31,080
...none of this...

340
00:38:31,700 --> 00:38:35,600
...will stop us from conquering Yenişehir.

341
00:38:39,760 --> 00:38:41,060
Osman Bey.

342
00:38:42,360 --> 00:38:44,480
I have been fighting for you all these
years.

343
00:38:44,800 --> 00:38:46,360
Before all...

344
00:38:47,380 --> 00:38:49,480
...I know you are a cautious person.

345
00:38:50,780 --> 00:38:54,740
Now, while Çobanoğulları Beys aren't
supporting us...

346
00:38:55,640 --> 00:38:58,740
...while a huge army is coming to attack
us...

347
00:38:59,400 --> 00:39:00,740
...is it time for conquest?

348
00:39:03,260 --> 00:39:04,780
I take a look and see that...

349
00:39:05,960 --> 00:39:08,140
...all beys are wondering about this.

350
00:39:08,620 --> 00:39:10,140
What is the rush?

351
00:39:12,000 --> 00:39:14,220
This is the greatest precaution.

352
00:39:15,040 --> 00:39:16,860
Emperor Andronikos...

353
00:39:17,220 --> 00:39:21,180
...gave the Yenişehir district to me
himself.

354
00:39:21,860 --> 00:39:25,560
Now, he will settle the army there.

355
00:39:26,080 --> 00:39:28,080
To strengthen his defense.

356
00:39:28,940 --> 00:39:30,940
How do you know this, Osman Bey?

357
00:39:32,060 --> 00:39:34,400
I know how to think with the mind of
my enemy.

358
00:39:35,400 --> 00:39:36,560
I am guessing.

359
00:39:38,020 --> 00:39:40,140
So, the reason for our rush is...

360
00:39:40,450 --> 00:39:42,530
...taking Yenişehir before it gets
stronger.

361
00:39:42,530 --> 00:39:44,280
Yes, it is.

362
00:39:44,700 --> 00:39:46,960
Now, an army is coming at us.

363
00:39:47,380 --> 00:39:51,100
But it is not the time to be afraid and
hide.

364
00:39:51,520 --> 00:39:54,520
If we hide...

365
00:39:55,160 --> 00:39:57,420
...we will face worse consequences.

366
00:40:00,080 --> 00:40:03,120
But, my Bey, you have two castles.

367
00:40:03,920 --> 00:40:06,720
We could gain the upper hand with
defensive warfare.

368
00:40:10,320 --> 00:40:11,120
My Bey.

369
00:40:14,200 --> 00:40:15,580
Barkın Bey.

370
00:40:18,460 --> 00:40:20,980
I grew up apart from my Bey due to
my duty.

371
00:40:22,180 --> 00:40:23,500
I grew up in the castles.

372
00:40:24,100 --> 00:40:25,840
I disguised as the infidels.

373
00:40:27,840 --> 00:40:29,340
But I never forgot something...

374
00:40:30,260 --> 00:40:33,720
...that you also know very well, Barkın
Bey...

375
00:40:34,860 --> 00:40:39,240
...defense is essential only when defeat
is imminent.

376
00:40:41,240 --> 00:40:43,380
It is never a preference.

377
00:40:44,260 --> 00:40:45,700
Attack...

378
00:40:47,060 --> 00:40:48,460
... if possible.

379
00:40:56,340 --> 00:40:57,580
Aktemur.

380
00:40:58,720 --> 00:41:00,020
Aktemur.

381
00:41:00,800 --> 00:41:04,100
Praise be! You are a befitting son
for your father.

382
00:41:06,320 --> 00:41:07,140
Thank you.

383
00:41:08,360 --> 00:41:10,520
If everyone sees fit...

384
00:41:11,060 --> 00:41:13,140
...if Osman Bey lets as well...

385
00:41:13,140 --> 00:41:16,460
...I will go to my tribe and talk to my
beys at once.

386
00:41:17,520 --> 00:41:22,080
Osman Bey, we support whatever your
order is.

387
00:41:24,180 --> 00:41:26,200
You've supported me all this time.

388
00:41:26,880 --> 00:41:28,200
Go back to your tribe now.

389
00:41:29,120 --> 00:41:31,320
And start the preparations for the war.

390
00:41:41,180 --> 00:41:42,600
Here you go.

391
00:41:53,300 --> 00:41:55,480
Let's see those prisoners.

392
00:42:01,780 --> 00:42:06,500
I hope it will be a healthy and mannerful
child, Bala Hatun.

393
00:42:06,500 --> 00:42:07,880
Amen!

394
00:42:08,120 --> 00:42:09,880
Thank you, my Servi.

395
00:42:21,220 --> 00:42:23,180
It is beautiful.

396
00:42:26,160 --> 00:42:28,300
Was I this little too, mother?

397
00:42:28,300 --> 00:42:29,180
Sure!

398
00:42:29,380 --> 00:42:31,340
You were a little baby.

399
00:42:31,340 --> 00:42:32,900
You were like an angel.

400
00:42:41,980 --> 00:42:44,080
My Ayşe, are you all right?

401
00:42:45,280 --> 00:42:47,000
Zehra, give her some water.

402
00:42:48,460 --> 00:42:49,600
Ayşe?

403
00:42:53,120 --> 00:42:54,380
Here, Ayşe Hatun.

404
00:42:54,800 --> 00:42:56,960
It must be that you haven't eaten
today.

405
00:42:57,480 --> 00:42:58,960
Should I prepare you some food?

406
00:43:03,600 --> 00:43:06,620
Would you like to get some air, Ayşe?

407
00:43:13,440 --> 00:43:17,140
Aygül, is there any news from the beys'
gathering?

408
00:43:21,740 --> 00:43:24,680
It is not over yet, Malhun.

409
00:43:29,640 --> 00:43:31,860
Ali Bey leaving us wasn't good at all.

410
00:43:33,860 --> 00:43:37,440
I wish Osman Bey would deliver Turgut Bey.

411
00:43:39,240 --> 00:43:41,080
You know Osman Bey, Servi.

412
00:43:41,920 --> 00:43:46,180
Let alone his brother Turgut Bey, he would
never deliver anyone without a trial.

413
00:43:47,500 --> 00:43:48,300
Also...

414
00:43:49,400 --> 00:43:51,900
...I don't believe Turgut Bey would do
such a thing.

415
00:43:54,400 --> 00:43:58,040
Turgut Bey is a smart man. He wouldn't
make a mistake like this.

416
00:44:00,180 --> 00:44:02,800
You know what happened before, sister.

417
00:44:04,160 --> 00:44:06,980
The truth comes out sooner or later.

418
00:44:07,500 --> 00:44:08,640
I hope so.

419
00:44:08,780 --> 00:44:11,900
We lived and learned our lesson,
thankfully.

420
00:44:13,480 --> 00:44:14,720
We did.

421
00:44:15,820 --> 00:44:19,880
Whoever couldn't stand Ali Bey's support
to Osman Bey...

422
00:44:20,960 --> 00:44:23,060
...must be involved in this.

423
00:44:25,600 --> 00:44:28,940
Protecting Turgut Bey until the truth is
revealed...

424
00:44:29,540 --> 00:44:31,600
...is Kayı Tribe's debt to him.

425
00:44:34,320 --> 00:44:36,080
You are right.

426
00:44:37,440 --> 00:44:41,200
Tugrut Bey and his tribe have always been
here for us in our darkest days.

427
00:44:41,600 --> 00:44:43,280
We owe them much.

428
00:44:58,460 --> 00:45:00,220
What is this?

429
00:45:05,660 --> 00:45:07,120
What is this?

430
00:45:07,480 --> 00:45:08,660
Open the door.

431
00:45:19,700 --> 00:45:21,220
What is this?

432
00:45:44,940 --> 00:45:46,120
Boran.

433
00:45:48,120 --> 00:45:49,440
Brothers.

434
00:45:50,840 --> 00:45:52,620
Is there some weakness in this tribe?

435
00:45:52,860 --> 00:45:55,380
How do they poison the prisoners
in the tent?

436
00:45:55,460 --> 00:45:57,229
We didn't let a bird fly, my Bey.

437
00:46:11,230 --> 00:46:13,880
They are the guardian alps, my Bey.

438
00:46:14,310 --> 00:46:17,400
These brothers were on the duty.

439
00:46:21,320 --> 00:46:23,310
Tell me.

440
00:46:23,530 --> 00:46:25,710
Tell me, alps. How could this happen?

441
00:46:25,840 --> 00:46:29,470
We are ready to take our punishment for our mistake, my Bey.

442
00:46:29,640 --> 00:46:32,620
But I swear no one came in or got out,
my Bey.

443
00:46:32,760 --> 00:46:36,270
Then how could this happen, brother?

444
00:46:37,210 --> 00:46:38,870
Stop, Boran.

445
00:46:40,530 --> 00:46:42,340
Stop for a second.

446
00:46:49,840 --> 00:46:51,380
Alps.

447
00:46:54,670 --> 00:46:56,590
Alps!

448
00:46:59,290 --> 00:47:01,860
Look at my face.

449
00:47:10,730 --> 00:47:13,390
I fully trust you.

450
00:47:14,860 --> 00:47:20,880
Obviously, there is something else behind
this.

451
00:47:22,320 --> 00:47:24,580
Do you think it is Cebe, my Bey?

452
00:47:27,240 --> 00:47:29,020
We will see.

453
00:47:29,850 --> 00:47:32,810
We will see, Cerkutay.

454
00:47:35,130 --> 00:47:36,570
We will see.

455
00:47:42,740 --> 00:47:44,510
Brothers.

456
00:47:48,250 --> 00:47:51,310
Since I thought you didn't fulfill your
duty, I got angry.

457
00:47:52,290 --> 00:47:54,820
Excuse my anger.

458
00:48:08,270 --> 00:48:11,820
I have never seen my father this angry,
brother.

459
00:48:13,670 --> 00:48:15,880
It is because of betrayal, brother.

460
00:48:16,220 --> 00:48:18,370
If they were poisoned while in tribe...

461
00:48:18,520 --> 00:48:20,710
...it means there is a traitor among us.

462
00:48:21,860 --> 00:48:25,150
But who would want to kill a rebel?

463
00:48:25,150 --> 00:48:29,370
I don't know brother. Time will show
the rest.

464
00:48:30,850 --> 00:48:32,940
My father didn't give Turgut Bey.

465
00:48:33,490 --> 00:48:35,020
He didn't but...

466
00:48:35,300 --> 00:48:37,410
...this will have a price, right?

467
00:48:37,660 --> 00:48:39,430
Of course, there will be, brother.

468
00:48:39,660 --> 00:48:42,790
But you know what our father taught us
before fighting.

469
00:48:43,850 --> 00:48:47,360
He who gives a sheep today gives his,
flock tomorrow.

470
00:48:47,870 --> 00:48:51,850
-Who gives his alp, his brother...
-...gives his beyship.

471
00:49:00,780 --> 00:49:03,350
Since the guardian alps didn't do it...

472
00:49:03,890 --> 00:49:06,820
...they can't be poisoned in our tribe.

473
00:49:08,230 --> 00:49:11,290
No one among the guardian alps would do
this, my Bey.

474
00:49:11,840 --> 00:49:13,800
We raised all of them ourselves.

475
00:49:15,780 --> 00:49:17,800
Either they have been poisoned before...

476
00:49:18,800 --> 00:49:21,260
...or they have poisoned themselves.

477
00:49:24,770 --> 00:49:29,470
Can we trust that Mongolian
commander, Cebe...

478
00:49:29,790 --> 00:49:31,880
...who brought the captives?

479
00:49:32,130 --> 00:49:34,130
The captives he brought in the morning...

480
00:49:34,300 --> 00:49:36,300
...died in the evening.

481
00:49:38,640 --> 00:49:41,980
Even the Seljuk Sultan cannot be trusted.

482
00:49:42,130 --> 00:49:43,580
But...

483
00:49:43,700 --> 00:49:46,470
...why would he poison the captives
he brought?

484
00:49:46,660 --> 00:49:49,420
If he was going to poison them,
why did he bring them?

485
00:49:49,810 --> 00:49:52,150
He wants to earn our trust.

486
00:49:53,300 --> 00:49:55,380
That is why.

487
00:49:57,950 --> 00:49:59,530
But...

488
00:50:00,140 --> 00:50:02,780
...he didn't let them talk.

489
00:50:03,720 --> 00:50:05,890
He is obviously up to something.

490
00:50:06,210 --> 00:50:08,500
Keep your eyes on him.

491
00:50:09,760 --> 00:50:11,820
Increase measures.

492
00:50:14,120 --> 00:50:16,910
Can I come in, Bey father?

493
00:50:17,140 --> 00:50:19,160
Come in, darling!

494
00:50:21,820 --> 00:50:23,070
Come here.

495
00:50:24,090 --> 00:50:25,600
Come here.

496
00:50:26,710 --> 00:50:28,690
I am sorry to interrupt.

497
00:50:28,820 --> 00:50:31,390
Don't mention. Here you go.

498
00:50:33,820 --> 00:50:35,280
My girl.

499
00:50:37,430 --> 00:50:38,860
Konur.

500
00:50:39,200 --> 00:50:40,490
Aktemur.

501
00:50:40,920 --> 00:50:43,000
Turgut Bey will go to the castle tomorrow.

502
00:50:43,170 --> 00:50:44,810
Increase the measures.

503
00:50:45,020 --> 00:50:46,940
Don't let anything happen to him.

504
00:50:47,110 --> 00:50:48,790
As you order, my Bey.

505
00:50:49,130 --> 00:50:51,960
-Will you excuse us?
-Sure.

506
00:51:00,620 --> 00:51:01,980
My baby.

507
00:51:03,700 --> 00:51:07,190
I wanted to see you before I go to sleep,
father.

508
00:51:09,550 --> 00:51:11,290
My darling.

509
00:51:11,530 --> 00:51:12,630
My baby.

510
00:51:12,800 --> 00:51:15,500
Did my sword begin to be forged?

511
00:51:15,760 --> 00:51:17,210
Look at this!

512
00:51:17,840 --> 00:51:19,350
Look at this!

513
00:51:21,350 --> 00:51:23,950
My beautiful girl. Don't worry.

514
00:51:24,100 --> 00:51:27,440
The most beautiful of swords will be
forged for you.

515
00:51:43,860 --> 00:51:51,020
Of! Of! My children! My children!

516
00:51:51,240 --> 00:51:53,300
This longing doesn't end!

517
00:51:54,360 --> 00:51:56,790
Oh, my Kayı, oh!

518
00:51:57,070 --> 00:52:01,020
I wish my Kayı was here to eat all
the food.

519
00:52:01,260 --> 00:52:03,890
I swear I wouldn't say anything.

520
00:52:04,640 --> 00:52:07,300
Of! Of!

521
00:52:17,990 --> 00:52:19,890
Cerkutay!

522
00:52:20,270 --> 00:52:24,310
What are you crying for? Your voice echoes
through the tribe.

523
00:52:26,180 --> 00:52:28,570
You bored and bored and bored
the children.

524
00:52:28,760 --> 00:52:30,710
Now they don't come back!

525
00:52:30,820 --> 00:52:32,480
Yes, Cerkutay. Yes.

526
00:52:32,630 --> 00:52:35,030
Is it even time for their return?

527
00:52:36,310 --> 00:52:40,880
Not your children but you are bored,
obviously.

528
00:52:41,200 --> 00:52:43,500
Yes, I am!

529
00:52:44,480 --> 00:52:46,430
I am bored!

530
00:52:46,650 --> 00:52:48,500
What kind of highland is this?

531
00:52:48,730 --> 00:52:50,980
My children are captives there!

532
00:52:52,200 --> 00:52:54,030
I am longing for them.

533
00:52:55,680 --> 00:52:59,920
Do you know what longing is?

534
00:53:00,320 --> 00:53:04,600
Cerkutay, get out!

535
00:53:04,750 --> 00:53:08,890
Don't get me mad!

536
00:53:14,470 --> 00:53:16,170
But...

537
00:53:22,210 --> 00:53:25,270
...if we had another child...

538
00:53:26,420 --> 00:53:29,630
...he would always be with us.

539
00:53:31,140 --> 00:53:33,520
He would always be by our sides.

540
00:53:35,650 --> 00:53:38,970
Right, my beautiful hatun?

541
00:53:49,690 --> 00:53:52,240
Stop, Aygül! Stop!

542
00:53:52,480 --> 00:53:53,820
Calm down!

543
00:53:54,200 --> 00:53:55,880
Breathe!

544
00:54:00,470 --> 00:54:02,300
Think again.

545
00:54:05,640 --> 00:54:06,830
Again.

546
00:54:07,450 --> 00:54:09,490
Get out, Cerkutay!

547
00:54:23,660 --> 00:54:25,440
You mad man!

548
00:54:25,850 --> 00:54:28,780
Kızılbeyoğlu Tribe

549
00:54:29,000 --> 00:54:31,610
No time has passed since the conquests.

550
00:54:31,820 --> 00:54:34,310
Will the people never rest?

551
00:54:34,780 --> 00:54:37,870
The horse's hooves that go fast are thrown
in four directions.

552
00:54:38,550 --> 00:54:40,560
The Turkmens couldn't get used to
this yet.

553
00:54:40,590 --> 00:54:44,030
We shouldn't look for anywhere else while
we haven't settled here yet.

554
00:54:44,990 --> 00:54:48,390
Your beys said. They are right as well.

555
00:54:48,930 --> 00:54:51,500
Do you have anything to say, Barkın Bey?

556
00:54:56,240 --> 00:54:59,820
Osman bey is great.

557
00:55:00,200 --> 00:55:03,200
But he is a dreamer.

558
00:55:03,710 --> 00:55:06,390
He tries things he can't afford.

559
00:55:06,600 --> 00:55:08,490
We've always said.

560
00:55:08,770 --> 00:55:10,000
Right?

561
00:55:10,340 --> 00:55:15,240
Praise be, he managed all his duties.

562
00:55:15,830 --> 00:55:17,130
But...

563
00:55:19,240 --> 00:55:23,360
...Osman Bey doesn't see Yenişehir as a
conquest.

564
00:55:24,320 --> 00:55:26,530
He sees it as a property fight.

565
00:55:27,760 --> 00:55:30,700
He says if we don't make Yenişehir a home
for the Turkmens...

566
00:55:30,700 --> 00:55:32,870
...we will lose what we have.

567
00:55:40,460 --> 00:55:41,500
You say...

568
00:55:42,700 --> 00:55:44,990
...we haven't seen peace and he says...

569
00:55:45,380 --> 00:55:49,820
...we won't have an eye to see it if we
don't take Yenişehir.

570
00:55:51,630 --> 00:55:54,820
You say the horse's shoes fall...

571
00:55:55,160 --> 00:55:57,950
...he says there will be no leg to run.

572
00:55:59,180 --> 00:56:00,860
Beys...

573
00:56:01,140 --> 00:56:06,820
...When Osman Bey says something,
you should think twice about it.

574
00:56:08,260 --> 00:56:10,350
Now we will wait...

575
00:56:10,620 --> 00:56:12,690
...and think.

576
00:56:13,430 --> 00:56:18,000
After a while, we will convey our decision
to Osman Bey.

577
00:56:26,170 --> 00:56:31,300
Those who attacked Ali Bey and killed
Atabey are the same.

578
00:56:32,130 --> 00:56:36,490
Although their disguises change,
their causes do not.

579
00:56:37,470 --> 00:56:42,590
Thus we will be more careful going to
the castle.

580
00:56:42,800 --> 00:56:44,680
-As you order, my Bey.
-As you order.

581
00:56:46,290 --> 00:56:47,680
Turgut Bey.

582
00:56:50,230 --> 00:56:52,570
Now they will try to attack you.

583
00:56:52,720 --> 00:56:55,350
Let them if they can, Osman Bey.

584
00:56:56,570 --> 00:57:02,690
But I don't understand why these dogs
disguise as Kayı alps.

585
00:57:02,900 --> 00:57:05,270
Why do they choose this way?

586
00:57:05,920 --> 00:57:08,820
The Mongols are of course involved.

587
00:57:09,180 --> 00:57:12,200
But they can't handle this alone.

588
00:57:13,390 --> 00:57:15,990
We have someone who knows his business.

589
00:57:16,330 --> 00:57:20,790
And as if that wasn't enough, they are
taking the hypocrites with us.

590
00:57:21,070 --> 00:57:23,450
Do you think Atabey is involved as well,
my Bey?

591
00:57:26,980 --> 00:57:30,130
What will it gain them by killing their
own allies?

592
00:57:30,130 --> 00:57:32,130
Let's say Atabey is a traitor.

593
00:57:32,640 --> 00:57:37,640
But wouldn't it be beneficial for them
to be alive when he infiltrated us much?

594
00:57:37,810 --> 00:57:39,320
No.

595
00:57:39,510 --> 00:57:41,570
We are now on bad terms with Ali Bey.

596
00:57:41,830 --> 00:57:43,960
This was what they wanted.

597
00:57:44,910 --> 00:57:48,340
Now the Çobanoğulları will get the other
beys' support too and...

598
00:57:48,700 --> 00:57:50,970
...point us as the enemy.

599
00:57:52,550 --> 00:57:59,040
They sacrificed Atabey Ahmed to stop
our struggle to be united.

600
00:57:59,290 --> 00:58:02,330
Ali Bey is a good man.
He has a pure heart.

601
00:58:02,630 --> 00:58:05,220
But even he was deceived by their dirty
games.

602
00:58:05,330 --> 00:58:07,610
Of course we know about their games.

603
00:58:07,780 --> 00:58:13,750
But even Ali Bey cannot see the truth
because of these traitors among us.

604
00:58:15,070 --> 00:58:20,520
Whoever this is, he is very close to us.

605
00:58:23,030 --> 00:58:25,050
And he hides himself so well.

606
00:58:25,900 --> 00:58:27,960
But we will find out.

607
00:58:28,580 --> 00:58:30,540
Of course, we will find out.

608
00:58:32,900 --> 00:58:37,960
Thanks to you, Turgut Bey.

609
00:58:38,260 --> 00:58:39,960
Thank you.

610
00:58:56,760 --> 00:58:57,970
Barkın!

611
00:58:58,530 --> 00:59:01,950
What are you doing here? Everyone thinks
you went to the tribe.

612
00:59:02,210 --> 00:59:05,010
Servi, I don't have much time.

613
00:59:05,160 --> 00:59:06,970
Have you got any important news?

614
00:59:10,970 --> 00:59:12,200
Servi?

615
00:59:17,610 --> 00:59:19,160
I did.

616
00:59:20,010 --> 00:59:23,090
They are taking Turgut Bey to
İnegöl Castle.

617
00:59:25,670 --> 00:59:28,430
I know Osman Bey would do such a mistake.

618
00:59:33,240 --> 00:59:34,300
Barkın.

619
00:59:35,940 --> 00:59:38,390
Malhun is my sister.

620
00:59:38,940 --> 00:59:41,850
You won't do anything that may harm them,
right?

621
00:59:42,750 --> 00:59:44,980
I am not doing anything, my Servi.

622
00:59:45,940 --> 00:59:51,360
But Osman Bey is very skillful at
attracting trouble.

623
00:59:51,720 --> 00:59:53,420
Not only himself but also...

624
00:59:53,660 --> 00:59:58,340
...he drags the tribe, us, your sister,
after himself.

625
01:00:03,850 --> 01:00:05,210
Selvi.

626
01:00:06,360 --> 01:00:08,270
Don't be sad.

627
01:00:08,820 --> 01:00:11,380
Don't worry.
I won't do anything.

628
01:00:11,610 --> 01:00:14,550
I will be silent for now.
I'll wait.

629
01:00:16,140 --> 01:00:17,840
You see?

630
01:00:18,310 --> 01:00:23,030
I think about our tribe and
Osman's reputation.

631
01:00:25,880 --> 01:00:27,730
I know, my bey.

632
01:00:30,880 --> 01:00:33,180
I know that you won't do wrong.

633
01:00:41,690 --> 01:00:44,300
Where is he?
Where?

634
01:00:45,540 --> 01:00:47,450
Where?

635
01:00:56,830 --> 01:00:58,120
Welcome, Barkın Bey.

636
01:01:01,740 --> 01:01:04,620
Barkın Bey, what's the situation?

637
01:01:10,850 --> 01:01:17,860
Osman Bey is secretly taking Turgut Bey
who tried to kill you, to İnegöl.

638
01:01:18,480 --> 01:01:20,290
Osman Bey...

639
01:01:22,140 --> 01:01:24,130
do you think it's that easy?

640
01:01:29,520 --> 01:01:30,410
İnegöl, huh?

641
01:01:30,830 --> 01:01:32,200
You know what to do...

642
01:01:32,200 --> 01:01:36,580
but be quick to gather
your men.

643
01:01:38,540 --> 01:01:41,400
You will be rewarded, Barkın Bey.

644
01:01:42,050 --> 01:01:43,890
I never forget a favor.

645
01:01:46,800 --> 01:01:49,210
Alps, come on!

646
01:02:00,180 --> 01:02:01,410
What will we do, my bey?

647
01:02:08,030 --> 01:02:09,740
We'll wait, Hüsamettin.

648
01:02:12,070 --> 01:02:13,420
We'll wait.

649
01:02:40,210 --> 01:02:41,740
Allah is eternal.

650
01:02:44,310 --> 01:02:46,130
Maybe we should stay away.

651
01:02:47,070 --> 01:02:48,950
He seems to be angry.

652
01:02:59,990 --> 01:03:02,990
If the father is a brand,
the children should be water.

653
01:03:04,240 --> 01:03:05,720
His anger will soothe.

654
01:03:11,800 --> 01:03:14,780
Father, we came to help you.

655
01:03:16,280 --> 01:03:19,120
Orhan. Alahaddin.

656
01:03:22,500 --> 01:03:25,820
Come here then.
Get your hammers.

657
01:03:28,190 --> 01:03:29,350
Hold it.

658
01:03:30,200 --> 01:03:31,350
My children.

659
01:03:34,530 --> 01:03:35,940
Allah is eternal!

660
01:03:36,640 --> 01:03:39,740
-Allah is eternal!
-Allah is righteous!

661
01:03:40,120 --> 01:03:41,740
Ya Allah!

662
01:03:41,740 --> 01:03:43,260
Allah is righteous!

663
01:03:43,260 --> 01:03:44,910
-Ya Allah!
-Allah is eternal!

664
01:03:44,910 --> 01:03:46,430
Allah is righteous!

665
01:03:46,550 --> 01:03:48,910
Wait now, my children.

666
01:03:50,540 --> 01:03:52,020
Wait now.

667
01:03:53,470 --> 01:03:55,630
Tell me, my children.

668
01:03:56,410 --> 01:03:58,350
What makes the steel strong?

669
01:03:58,730 --> 01:04:00,350
The powerful strikes.

670
01:04:01,160 --> 01:04:02,720
Only that?

671
01:04:05,150 --> 01:04:06,730
The water too.

672
01:04:08,200 --> 01:04:09,600
My children.

673
01:04:13,590 --> 01:04:17,470
You will take the weapon first...

674
01:04:18,250 --> 01:04:20,160
warm it up...

675
01:04:21,130 --> 01:04:22,650
it'll turn aestuous...

676
01:04:23,510 --> 01:04:28,110
then, you'll start forging it...

677
01:04:30,520 --> 01:04:32,080
you'll forge it...

678
01:04:35,160 --> 01:04:38,620
you'll forge it,
and you'll forge it!

679
01:04:39,460 --> 01:04:43,950
And you'll leave it to cool down.

680
01:04:46,830 --> 01:04:51,550
But you won't forget to
speak Allah's name.

681
01:04:53,520 --> 01:04:55,650
That also will always be
with you.

682
01:04:56,150 --> 01:05:00,140
So, you will have a companion...

683
01:05:01,000 --> 01:05:05,020
and you will have a good weapon.

684
01:05:06,800 --> 01:05:11,270
Only the brave enemies are
afraid of a weapon.

685
01:05:12,100 --> 01:05:16,030
Only those who face you with
their arms.

686
01:05:17,020 --> 01:05:22,190
Otherwise, this weapon has no
meaning.

687
01:05:25,600 --> 01:05:26,900
Who else?

688
01:05:27,410 --> 01:05:31,850
The treacherous backstabbers?

689
01:05:31,850 --> 01:05:34,610
Yes, son. Yes.

690
01:05:34,850 --> 01:05:41,450
But only one weapon works
on them.

691
01:05:44,010 --> 01:05:44,760
Smart.

692
01:05:48,500 --> 01:05:50,020
It's the word of our ancestors.

693
01:05:50,300 --> 01:05:54,640
Even if your enemy is coming
with a stick...

694
01:05:55,140 --> 01:05:57,790
you'll bring a steel shield.

695
01:06:02,110 --> 01:06:05,340
My children, come.

696
01:06:06,600 --> 01:06:08,070
Come now.

697
01:06:10,780 --> 01:06:13,370
You'll always be cautious.

698
01:06:14,580 --> 01:06:16,990
Victories won't make us careless.

699
01:06:18,030 --> 01:06:21,240
Our sleep is the sleep of a rabbit.
Carelessness can stay away.

700
01:06:21,240 --> 01:06:22,700
Mashallah.

701
01:06:23,270 --> 01:06:25,900
We'll sharpen our weapon
that is the smart, father.

702
01:06:25,900 --> 01:06:27,900
Mashallah to my valiants.

703
01:06:28,660 --> 01:06:29,900
Mashallah.

704
01:06:31,210 --> 01:06:32,810
A wolf's child is a wolf, my bey.

705
01:06:35,720 --> 01:06:37,720
Mashallah to my bey's children.

706
01:06:40,020 --> 01:06:42,860
My bey, beys want to speak.

707
01:06:44,150 --> 01:06:45,360
Let them wait.

708
01:06:46,190 --> 01:06:48,720
-I'll come soon.
-Yes, my bey.

709
01:06:51,250 --> 01:06:55,620
When the foal grows up,
the horse rests...

710
01:06:56,320 --> 01:06:58,420
when the children grow up,
the bet rests.

711
01:07:00,100 --> 01:07:01,160
My children.

712
01:07:03,280 --> 01:07:06,900
You won't leave here until you
turn this steel into a weapon.

713
01:07:07,700 --> 01:07:10,880
This steel will be Fatma's weapon.

714
01:07:11,770 --> 01:07:12,710
Come on now.

715
01:07:13,720 --> 01:07:14,710
Yes, my bey.

716
01:07:15,440 --> 01:07:17,070
Thank you.
Thank you.

717
01:07:36,840 --> 01:07:38,400
I hope it's good news.

718
01:07:38,560 --> 01:07:41,500
My bey, good and bad comes
from Allah.

719
01:07:41,500 --> 01:07:43,500
We are just messengers.

720
01:07:44,070 --> 01:07:46,900
Tell me, what's the result
of the council?

721
01:07:49,450 --> 01:07:50,520
They abstain, my bey.

722
01:07:51,480 --> 01:07:55,430
They say prosperity, comfort,
resting...

723
01:07:56,120 --> 01:07:59,960
their hearts are with us but
their minds need convincing.

724
01:08:01,430 --> 01:08:05,380
We are running out of time.
We have to solve it soon.

725
01:08:05,860 --> 01:08:09,700
After this trial,
that will be done too.

726
01:08:13,290 --> 01:08:14,640
Beys are waiting.

727
01:08:15,569 --> 01:08:17,029
I'm going now.

728
01:08:24,800 --> 01:08:28,450
The only thing that will be done
is you, Osman.

729
01:08:43,479 --> 01:08:46,020
Behold! Osman Bey!

730
01:09:06,859 --> 01:09:08,200
Go on.

731
01:09:13,540 --> 01:09:20,790
You are also opposed to my Yenişehir
move, just like Barkın Bey's beys.

732
01:09:24,149 --> 01:09:25,410
Now, tell me...

733
01:09:27,020 --> 01:09:28,350
I'm listening.

734
01:09:29,300 --> 01:09:32,590
A council is for the opposition,
for exchange of views.

735
01:09:32,850 --> 01:09:36,120
Even if there is nothing else,
the people are unsafe.

736
01:09:36,600 --> 01:09:39,970
Your greatest commander Gündüz Bey
is a martyr.

737
01:09:40,649 --> 01:09:42,600
Turgut Bey is wounded.

738
01:09:42,600 --> 01:09:45,960
Ali Bey who came to aid you
is now against you.

739
01:09:47,819 --> 01:09:51,109
Osman Bey, you only speak
of your victories.

740
01:09:51,450 --> 01:09:54,149
What about the losses?
The missing?

741
01:09:55,130 --> 01:09:56,720
Demir Bey is right.

742
01:10:02,820 --> 01:10:04,940
My bey, we know your vision.

743
01:10:04,940 --> 01:10:07,030
We don't want to root here.

744
01:10:07,400 --> 01:10:08,840
But the people are tired.

745
01:10:10,610 --> 01:10:13,590
Osman Bey, Turgut Bey's trial
should be over.

746
01:10:14,230 --> 01:10:18,190
There should be peace with
Ali Bey. We should regather our strength.

747
01:10:18,660 --> 01:10:21,940
Then, tell us to ride and we'll
ride to hell.

748
01:10:22,470 --> 01:10:24,720
But we need to wait now.

749
01:10:34,110 --> 01:10:36,000
It must be a while since Gencebay
went.

750
01:10:36,640 --> 01:10:38,730
Do you think he's settled, brother?

751
01:10:38,730 --> 01:10:41,330
He was with Osman Bey
longer than us.

752
01:10:41,330 --> 01:10:42,670
His training is complete.

753
01:10:43,030 --> 01:10:44,940
He must be fine.

754
01:10:48,190 --> 01:10:51,160
Incoming! They have Seljuk flags.

755
01:11:19,050 --> 01:11:20,430
Open the gates!

756
01:12:03,910 --> 01:12:05,960
This is what concern us, my bey.

757
01:12:05,960 --> 01:12:10,170
After this smoke cloud goes,
we'll go anywhere you say.

758
01:12:11,520 --> 01:12:12,510
Thank you.

759
01:12:13,140 --> 01:12:15,780
I listened to you without
uttering a single word.

760
01:12:17,780 --> 01:12:22,140
But I'll speak briefly.

761
01:12:23,590 --> 01:12:26,130
My move isn't desperate for persuasion.

762
01:12:26,570 --> 01:12:28,910
Jihad doesn't happen with persuasion.

763
01:12:29,560 --> 01:12:36,430
Now, before the emperor moves
with his army, I'll take Yenişehir.

764
01:12:37,720 --> 01:12:42,900
When I spur my horse, I won't
look behind.

765
01:12:45,570 --> 01:12:48,810
-May I enter, my bey?
-Come in.

766
01:12:54,050 --> 01:12:57,690
A commander came from Konya.
He wants to see you.

767
01:13:05,030 --> 01:13:06,570
Let him in.

768
01:13:20,340 --> 01:13:21,990
Welcome.

769
01:13:22,440 --> 01:13:25,920
You took a long road.
Come, rest here.

770
01:13:25,920 --> 01:13:28,580
Osman Bey, I don't have much time.

771
01:13:29,280 --> 01:13:31,990
I'll return before my horse's
sweat dries.

772
01:13:33,620 --> 01:13:37,170
By Sultan Alahaddin's order,
I came to take Turgut Bey.

773
01:13:44,310 --> 01:13:49,380
Asking the impossible doesn't fit
a smart soldier.

774
01:13:49,690 --> 01:13:53,560
It's not asking, Osman Bey.
It's the sultan's order.

775
01:13:55,060 --> 01:13:56,800
Asking or ordering.

776
01:13:59,590 --> 01:14:01,950
It doesn't make the impossible
more possible.

777
01:14:03,730 --> 01:14:05,530
The trial will be here.

778
01:14:06,260 --> 01:14:10,530
Osman Bey, you speak as a revolter.

779
01:14:13,560 --> 01:14:15,920
Don't make me use force.

780
01:14:17,280 --> 01:14:18,580
Behold!

781
01:14:21,740 --> 01:14:22,890
Now...

782
01:14:24,300 --> 01:14:27,090
send my thanks to Sultan Alahaddin.

783
01:14:28,320 --> 01:14:35,060
But we will solve our internal issues
inside.

784
01:14:37,060 --> 01:14:39,600
If you mean to use force...

785
01:14:39,840 --> 01:14:44,950
you can't even reach Konya to
carry the news.

786
01:14:48,280 --> 01:14:50,370
The emperor is coming for you.

787
01:14:51,020 --> 01:14:54,020
When it's so soon that you'll
beg for help from the emperor...

788
01:14:54,520 --> 01:14:57,840
you are revolting against the state
for a criminal.

789
01:14:58,660 --> 01:15:06,980
Here, I'm the bey.
And I'm the state!

790
01:15:08,600 --> 01:15:10,300
Now get out of my sight!

791
01:15:33,020 --> 01:15:36,690
You did your job.
Now go and carry the bey's answer.

792
01:15:37,630 --> 01:15:39,310
I know Konya and Kayı.

793
01:15:40,360 --> 01:15:42,420
Do as I say.
Don't push it.

794
01:15:43,450 --> 01:15:48,340
So, you are the fool who turned
his back to the state to obey a bey.

795
01:15:56,300 --> 01:15:58,190
Watch your words.

796
01:15:58,190 --> 01:16:00,770
And keep your eyes on the truth,
commander.

797
01:16:01,490 --> 01:16:02,960
Go to Konya now.

798
01:16:03,600 --> 01:16:05,320
You are playing with fire.

799
01:16:05,380 --> 01:16:09,920
Yes. We are the fire.
Don't get too close.

800
01:16:10,990 --> 01:16:11,860
Go.

801
01:16:29,420 --> 01:16:31,380
What will happen now?

802
01:16:32,120 --> 01:16:33,930
The situation isn't good.

803
01:16:40,580 --> 01:16:42,900
The sun blinded you.

804
01:16:45,270 --> 01:16:47,880
You are stuck in the dirt.
You can't get out.

805
01:16:50,320 --> 01:16:52,450
There is only one move to make.

806
01:16:54,030 --> 01:16:55,430
And it's Yenişehir.

807
01:16:57,840 --> 01:17:02,890
Either you are with me,
or you are with no one.

808
01:17:16,360 --> 01:17:17,910
Good day!

809
01:17:17,910 --> 01:17:19,170
Good day, sisters!

810
01:17:19,170 --> 01:17:21,830
Thank you!
Thank you!

811
01:17:23,050 --> 01:17:26,000
Alaca, is people's provisions
ready?

812
01:17:26,000 --> 01:17:27,580
Everything is ready, Malhun Hatun.

813
01:17:27,580 --> 01:17:28,580
Mashallah.

814
01:17:28,580 --> 01:17:32,400
People will lack nothing
before the eid qurban.

815
01:17:33,120 --> 01:17:36,110
Then, let's be on our way
and do our duty.

816
01:17:37,120 --> 01:17:40,110
Sister, let me come with you
to Söğüt.

817
01:17:40,110 --> 01:17:42,110
I want to have my part
in this good deed.

818
01:17:42,110 --> 01:17:43,980
I'll go to the tribe
on the return.

819
01:17:43,980 --> 01:17:45,000
Sure, sister.

820
01:17:45,660 --> 01:17:47,000
Come on then.

821
01:18:01,150 --> 01:18:02,520
Ayşe!

822
01:18:04,870 --> 01:18:07,710
Ayşe! Ayşe!
Ayşe!

823
01:18:07,710 --> 01:18:08,930
Enough!

824
01:18:10,330 --> 01:18:12,140
Do you want to die?

825
01:18:12,760 --> 01:18:14,140
You are pale again!

826
01:18:14,140 --> 01:18:16,420
You are pale again!
Let's go to the infirmary.

827
01:18:16,420 --> 01:18:18,280
Come on, to the infirmary.

828
01:18:19,640 --> 01:18:21,600
Ayşe!

829
01:18:22,790 --> 01:18:23,600
Ayşe!

830
01:18:25,480 --> 01:18:26,720
Aygül, what happened?

831
01:18:26,720 --> 01:18:29,730
I speak but she doesn't listen.
You talk to her!

832
01:18:30,230 --> 01:18:33,310
She keeps working.
She was about to faint.

833
01:18:34,800 --> 01:18:36,610
Don't do this to yourself, Ayşe.

834
01:18:37,130 --> 01:18:39,960
You didn't speak a word since
Gündüz Bey has fallen.

835
01:18:44,180 --> 01:18:46,820
You are tearing inside instead
of outside, Ayşe.

836
01:18:47,460 --> 01:18:50,930
You don't pity yourself,
what about your child?

837
01:18:52,040 --> 01:18:54,660
Girls, bring some water!

838
01:18:56,760 --> 01:18:58,820
Malhun, it's time.
Go to Söğüt.

839
01:18:58,820 --> 01:19:00,320
We'll catch up.

840
01:19:00,980 --> 01:19:03,860
You are right. We need to be
there for salaat.

841
01:19:03,860 --> 01:19:04,980
Come on, women.

842
01:19:05,350 --> 01:19:06,200
Ayşe.

843
01:19:08,200 --> 01:19:08,980
Come on.

844
01:19:09,550 --> 01:19:12,050
Alps. We are on our way.

845
01:19:14,330 --> 01:19:16,530
She is powerless.

846
01:19:16,680 --> 01:19:18,750
Let's go to the infirmary.

847
01:19:23,170 --> 01:19:24,190
She doesn't want it.

848
01:19:25,300 --> 01:19:28,760
You don't pity yourself,
what about your baby?

849
01:19:31,918 --> 01:19:33,220
Baby?

850
01:19:37,040 --> 01:19:37,880
Ayşe?

851
01:19:46,480 --> 01:19:48,040
Allah's grace!

852
01:19:49,220 --> 01:19:51,640
But why didn't you say it
all this time?

853
01:19:52,040 --> 01:19:53,860
Is it something to hide?

854
01:19:56,860 --> 01:19:58,540
Ayşe didn't want it.

855
01:19:59,100 --> 01:20:00,880
But it's time, sister.

856
01:20:04,780 --> 01:20:06,620
Gündüz Bey's gift.

857
01:20:07,860 --> 01:20:10,000
Thank Allah!

858
01:20:10,740 --> 01:20:13,460
Come on, Ayşe.
You should protect your baby.

859
01:20:13,620 --> 01:20:15,260
To the infirmary.

860
01:20:15,560 --> 01:20:18,280
Come on, let's leave you to
the girls.

861
01:20:19,680 --> 01:20:20,620
Come on.

862
01:20:27,040 --> 01:20:28,640
I'm going to İnegöl but...

863
01:20:29,300 --> 01:20:31,140
I don't feel good about it.

864
01:20:32,020 --> 01:20:36,180
We are doing what we need
to do for justice.

865
01:20:36,260 --> 01:20:37,700
Be at ease.

866
01:20:38,920 --> 01:20:43,120
With all the trouble we have,
now we are facing the sultan.

867
01:20:44,980 --> 01:20:48,400
I'm afraid that he'll take Söğüt
and İnegöl after all the trouble.

868
01:20:49,360 --> 01:20:50,400
Because of me.

869
01:20:50,760 --> 01:20:55,000
Where we stand is justice
and truth.

870
01:20:55,880 --> 01:20:58,320
It doesn't matter where
they stand.

871
01:20:59,100 --> 01:21:00,620
Surely, my bey.

872
01:21:01,460 --> 01:21:02,620
Surely.

873
01:21:04,160 --> 01:21:05,200
Osman Bey.

874
01:21:06,120 --> 01:21:07,440
I know that you protect me.

875
01:21:07,980 --> 01:21:11,820
But allow me to surrender in Konya.
I'll return alive, don't worry.

876
01:21:11,880 --> 01:21:13,360
I'm sure of myself.

877
01:21:13,360 --> 01:21:18,640
Turgut, for sultan to see the truth,
you won't surrender now.

878
01:21:19,500 --> 01:21:21,580
So, you will go to İnegöl.

879
01:21:22,880 --> 01:21:26,680
If I surrender you now...

880
01:21:27,300 --> 01:21:31,040
then, I'll be betraying
justice and truth.

881
01:21:35,200 --> 01:21:36,280
The trial...

882
01:21:38,460 --> 01:21:40,160
will be held in İnegöl.

883
01:21:40,640 --> 01:21:42,720
Osman Bey has spoken.

884
01:21:43,400 --> 01:21:47,860
Then, we should go to İnegöl.

885
01:21:52,160 --> 01:21:52,880
My bey.

886
01:21:54,300 --> 01:21:56,940
News from Kumral Abdal
and Master Davud.

887
01:22:11,780 --> 01:22:13,580
It's bad news.

888
01:22:15,720 --> 01:22:17,600
There is an army in Yenişehir.

889
01:22:18,200 --> 01:22:20,180
It might move any time.

890
01:22:22,480 --> 01:22:24,020
What are your orders, my bey?

891
01:22:27,200 --> 01:22:29,500
We'll be working soon.

892
01:22:32,460 --> 01:22:36,020
Be careful, Ayşe Hatun.
You are tiring yourself too much.

893
01:22:36,280 --> 01:22:38,840
Your pregnancy is certain now.

894
01:22:46,600 --> 01:22:47,540
Mother?

895
01:23:10,780 --> 01:23:13,540
Is it true, mother?

896
01:23:18,080 --> 01:23:19,060
My sibling...

897
01:23:23,840 --> 01:23:25,820
Do I have a sibling, mother?

898
01:23:35,520 --> 01:23:37,000
My beautiful mother!

899
01:23:40,280 --> 01:23:41,920
My father's gift.

900
01:23:44,360 --> 01:23:45,160
You...

901
01:23:46,600 --> 01:23:48,560
is this why you were silent
all this time?

902
01:23:51,660 --> 01:23:53,840
Why didn't you tell me, mother?

903
01:23:57,180 --> 01:23:58,520
Cry, mother.
Cry.

904
01:24:00,240 --> 01:24:01,940
Crying isn't shameful.

905
01:24:03,940 --> 01:24:05,840
Your crying isn't from rebellion.

906
01:24:07,840 --> 01:24:10,780
It's from longing.

907
01:24:16,320 --> 01:24:18,340
Don't leave us without you, mother.

908
01:24:20,340 --> 01:24:22,240
Who else do we have?

909
01:24:24,940 --> 01:24:26,500
Aktimur.

910
01:24:28,500 --> 01:24:30,000
Aktimur!

911
01:24:34,820 --> 01:24:37,680
Tell me, mother.
Tell me.

912
01:24:40,940 --> 01:24:43,080
-My son.
-Mother!

913
01:24:43,940 --> 01:24:45,080
My son!

914
01:24:45,980 --> 01:24:47,980
My beloved mother!

915
01:24:50,100 --> 01:24:53,960
I was so afraid to not hear
your voice again.

916
01:24:54,620 --> 01:24:56,760
Thank Allah.

917
01:25:02,680 --> 01:25:05,300
I couldn't be sure earlier.

918
01:25:06,340 --> 01:25:08,460
I didn't want to believe it.

919
01:25:09,640 --> 01:25:15,520
When the midwife told me,
I ran to the tent...

920
01:25:18,300 --> 01:25:20,520
but I couldn't find your father.

921
01:25:22,980 --> 01:25:24,460
I couldn't!

922
01:25:29,240 --> 01:25:30,740
I couldn't!

923
01:25:37,120 --> 01:25:41,260
I'm so much in pain.

924
01:25:41,500 --> 01:25:42,780
So much.

925
01:25:43,020 --> 01:25:46,080
I couldn't speak out of fear.

926
01:25:48,480 --> 01:25:49,840
All that time...

927
01:25:51,600 --> 01:25:54,340
your father and I wanted
a baby.

928
01:25:55,980 --> 01:25:57,720
We waited for that...

929
01:25:58,680 --> 01:26:04,200
but your sibling couldn't
come in time for your father.

930
01:26:08,300 --> 01:26:09,460
My light...

931
01:26:10,700 --> 01:26:13,540
my sunlight.
He couldn't...

932
01:26:15,300 --> 01:26:17,280
know his child.

933
01:26:18,220 --> 01:26:20,120
He couldn't see...

934
01:26:22,600 --> 01:26:23,900
It's a trial, mother.

935
01:26:25,240 --> 01:26:27,060
This is our trial.

936
01:26:28,620 --> 01:26:32,360
But don't worry.
I'll protect my sibling.

937
01:26:35,100 --> 01:26:37,520
I know, son.
I know.

938
01:26:38,040 --> 01:26:39,520
My brave son.

939
01:26:41,740 --> 01:26:46,780
You shined my day with your
beautiful voice, mother.

940
01:26:47,820 --> 01:26:50,100
Today is a holiday for me!

941
01:26:55,960 --> 01:26:57,040
My beautiful mother.

942
01:26:59,860 --> 01:27:01,680
Duty awaits.

943
01:27:02,460 --> 01:27:03,680
I'll go.

944
01:27:05,020 --> 01:27:09,420
But I'll come back to hear
your voice again.

945
01:27:10,800 --> 01:27:12,520
May Allah protect you.

946
01:27:13,580 --> 01:27:14,520
Thank you, mother.

947
01:27:36,100 --> 01:27:37,680
Gündüz...

948
01:27:40,120 --> 01:27:41,680
It wasn't destined.

949
01:27:42,700 --> 01:27:43,940
You couldn't know...

950
01:27:45,500 --> 01:27:46,800
couldn't see...

951
01:27:48,080 --> 01:27:51,860
but we'll have another child.

952
01:27:53,700 --> 01:27:55,620
You always wanted it.

953
01:28:23,020 --> 01:28:25,180
Cerkutay is tracking, right?

954
01:28:25,600 --> 01:28:27,180
He is.

955
01:28:37,180 --> 01:28:38,920
Turgut!

956
01:28:39,780 --> 01:28:42,380
You'll answer for killing my atabey!

957
01:28:44,380 --> 01:28:46,300
You'll die in pain!

958
01:28:50,620 --> 01:28:54,280
Turgut Bey moved out to the castle.
They are coming closer.

959
01:28:55,860 --> 01:28:57,160
Let him come.

960
01:28:57,740 --> 01:28:59,160
He is coming to his death.

961
01:29:14,600 --> 01:29:17,680
Turgut moved out to the castle.

962
01:29:18,440 --> 01:29:22,180
And Mustafa moved to stop them.

963
01:29:24,720 --> 01:29:26,060
It's time.

964
01:29:27,240 --> 01:29:30,040
Once Osman gets Mustafa's
blood on his hands...

965
01:29:30,840 --> 01:29:33,040
no one can hold Ali Bey back.

966
01:29:33,280 --> 01:29:37,940
Then, neither Osman nor the Kayı
Tribe will survive.

967
01:29:38,680 --> 01:29:40,540
Mongols on the other side...

968
01:29:42,080 --> 01:29:46,220
we'll remove Osman from these lands.

969
01:29:46,980 --> 01:29:48,980
All the arrows point to one target.

970
01:29:49,620 --> 01:29:50,980
Osman.

971
01:29:51,280 --> 01:29:54,500
Even if he survives one,
he won't survive the other.

972
01:29:54,900 --> 01:29:57,760
Cebe is impatient for it,
Commander Romanos.

973
01:29:58,060 --> 01:29:59,420
He is waiting.

974
01:29:59,880 --> 01:30:01,420
Right.

975
01:30:02,280 --> 01:30:04,940
Let's not keep the Mongol
wildling waiting.

976
01:30:30,360 --> 01:30:31,260
Who are you?

977
01:30:33,260 --> 01:30:35,300
Who are you swinging your
swords for?

978
01:30:36,900 --> 01:30:38,160
I'm talking to you!

979
01:30:51,880 --> 01:30:53,920
For me!

980
01:31:09,100 --> 01:31:11,700
My atabey's murdeer, Turgut!

981
01:31:11,960 --> 01:31:14,000
It's time to answer now!

982
01:31:15,780 --> 01:31:17,920
You all will answer!

983
01:31:21,700 --> 01:31:22,800
A trap!

984
01:31:23,420 --> 01:31:24,500
A trap!

985
01:31:24,580 --> 01:31:26,280
Alps! Attack!

986
01:32:02,580 --> 01:32:04,200
Turgut!

987
01:32:06,680 --> 01:32:08,720
Osman Bey!

988
01:32:18,900 --> 01:32:20,780
Come at me, Osman Bey!

989
01:32:43,980 --> 01:32:47,960
The game of the jackals last
until the wolves howl.

990
01:32:49,000 --> 01:32:51,080
You want to take revenge, huh?

991
01:32:51,500 --> 01:32:52,720
But...

992
01:32:53,720 --> 01:32:55,320
but you are in my hands now.

993
01:32:55,620 --> 01:32:59,980
You can't kill me. You are afraid
of my father, Osman Bey.

994
01:33:02,280 --> 01:33:03,860
You can't touch me.

995
01:33:40,760 --> 01:33:42,640
The traces lead to Söğüt.

996
01:33:55,820 --> 01:33:57,960
It might be a trap, Cerkutay Alp!

997
01:34:10,820 --> 01:34:12,240
Aygül.

998
01:34:14,400 --> 01:34:15,840
Women.

999
01:34:16,840 --> 01:34:19,800
They went to Söğüt to take
provisions there.

1000
01:34:20,000 --> 01:34:23,200
It's a trap!
It's a trap, alps!

1001
01:34:25,560 --> 01:34:29,460
I'm the heir of the Çobanoğlu Tribe!

1002
01:34:34,460 --> 01:34:36,020
You are naive.

1003
01:34:37,360 --> 01:34:38,800
You are naive, son.

1004
01:34:39,960 --> 01:34:43,760
But it's apparent that your
atabey played you.

1005
01:34:45,140 --> 01:34:48,840
I need whoever your atabey Ahmet
was working with.

1006
01:34:49,420 --> 01:34:51,440
No one deceived me!

1007
01:34:51,920 --> 01:34:54,780
Don't speak of my atabey's name!

1008
01:34:55,200 --> 01:34:58,960
I'll avenge him, Osman Bey!

1009
01:35:01,860 --> 01:35:04,800
I only answer to Allah.

1010
01:35:05,540 --> 01:35:09,000
But you will answer me first...

1011
01:35:10,240 --> 01:35:12,480
and then your father.

1012
01:35:20,160 --> 01:35:24,200
Since Gündüz Bey has fallen,
Ayşe was buried in darkness.

1013
01:35:24,420 --> 01:35:25,500
It's hard, sister.

1014
01:35:25,960 --> 01:35:29,140
What can be worse than
losing your lover?

1015
01:35:30,660 --> 01:35:32,200
Surely, it's hard.

1016
01:35:32,200 --> 01:35:36,480
But together, we'll take Ayşe
out of darkness, inshallah.

1017
01:35:36,940 --> 01:35:38,480
Inshallah, sister.

1018
01:35:40,480 --> 01:35:41,660
Come on.

1019
01:35:47,460 --> 01:35:50,120
Alps! Take position!

1020
01:35:52,380 --> 01:35:53,600
Selvi!

1021
01:35:54,800 --> 01:35:56,280
Selvi! Sister!

1022
01:35:56,740 --> 01:35:58,880
Sister!

1023
01:36:06,260 --> 01:36:07,620
Kill them all!

1024
01:36:17,660 --> 01:36:18,840
Are you alright?

1025
01:36:18,840 --> 01:36:21,200
I'm fine, sister.
I'm fine.

1026
01:36:28,040 --> 01:36:29,300
You were right.

1027
01:36:29,300 --> 01:36:31,640
There is no end to the enemies
on the borders.

1028
01:36:31,640 --> 01:36:32,680
There isn't.

1029
01:36:32,680 --> 01:36:35,760
As long as there are wolves,
there will be dogs too.

1030
01:36:40,000 --> 01:36:42,220
Alaca! We are leaving.

1031
01:36:42,220 --> 01:36:43,600
Come on, Selvi!

1032
01:36:44,940 --> 01:36:46,720
Selvi! Selvi!

1033
01:36:47,920 --> 01:36:49,420
Alps!

1034
01:36:51,840 --> 01:36:53,560
Follow those women!

1035
01:37:06,560 --> 01:37:09,560
I can't--
I can't breathe, Osman Bey.

1036
01:37:13,080 --> 01:37:14,460
Son.

1037
01:37:17,300 --> 01:37:19,820
It's apparent that your
atabey deceived you.

1038
01:37:20,200 --> 01:37:24,000
He tried slandering Turgut.

1039
01:37:25,800 --> 01:37:27,540
You are lying!

1040
01:37:28,460 --> 01:37:30,520
It's all your pride!

1041
01:37:32,260 --> 01:37:34,460
You want to be the head of the Turks.

1042
01:37:35,140 --> 01:37:39,400
You will do anything for that, Osman Bey!

1043
01:37:43,500 --> 01:37:46,080
Son. Look.

1044
01:37:47,780 --> 01:37:49,620
You don't know anything.

1045
01:37:50,380 --> 01:37:52,420
You are deceived.

1046
01:38:05,160 --> 01:38:07,580
Hang on, sister.
Hang on.

1047
01:38:08,480 --> 01:38:09,860
A little more.

1048
01:38:18,800 --> 01:38:20,520
Selvi!

1049
01:38:21,600 --> 01:38:23,440
Alaca, protect Selvi!

1050
01:38:29,270 --> 01:38:36,070
Women, today we either live
together or die together!

1051
01:38:55,980 --> 01:38:57,810
Selvi! Sister!

1052
01:38:57,810 --> 01:39:00,470
Sister! Sister!
Please, hang on!

1053
01:39:00,470 --> 01:39:01,700
I'll save you.

1054
01:39:01,700 --> 01:39:04,550
Selvi! I'll get you to the tribe!

1055
01:39:04,550 --> 01:39:06,550
Alaca, protect Selvi!

1056
01:39:28,500 --> 01:39:30,240
Hang on, Malhun!

1057
01:39:39,070 --> 01:39:40,670
Selvi!

1058
01:39:41,120 --> 01:39:42,440
Selvi!

1059
01:39:42,440 --> 01:39:45,350
Selvi, sister!
Please, hear me!

1060
01:39:45,350 --> 01:39:47,350
Please, don't give up!

1061
01:39:48,240 --> 01:39:50,840
Hang on, please!

1062
01:40:07,980 --> 01:40:08,870
Malhun!

1063
01:40:09,780 --> 01:40:12,100
Malhun!

1064
01:40:12,100 --> 01:40:14,100
Selvi!

1065
01:40:17,120 --> 01:40:18,780
Are you alright?

1066
01:40:19,640 --> 01:40:22,040
Mashallah, sisters.
You didn't leave any for us!

1067
01:40:22,040 --> 01:40:24,120
It's no time to joke!
We have wounded.

1068
01:40:24,120 --> 01:40:25,870
I won't, my wife.
I won't.

1069
01:40:25,870 --> 01:40:27,870
Run this way!

1070
01:40:27,870 --> 01:40:29,120
Alps, come on!

1071
01:40:29,120 --> 01:40:30,040
Come on!

1072
01:40:30,780 --> 01:40:32,920
Bring the carts!

1073
01:40:32,920 --> 01:40:33,670
Malhun!

1074
01:40:33,670 --> 01:40:36,410
Sister! Sister!
Please, hang on!

1075
01:40:36,410 --> 01:40:38,180
Hang on, please!

1076
01:40:38,180 --> 01:40:39,780
Malhun, you are wounded.

1077
01:40:39,780 --> 01:40:40,980
It's not important!

1078
01:40:41,320 --> 01:40:45,780
Selvi! Hang on!
Hang on! Hang on, sister!

1079
01:40:46,210 --> 01:40:47,470
Don't leave me!

1080
01:40:47,470 --> 01:40:49,470
Selvi!

1081
01:40:57,500 --> 01:40:58,780
Now, tell me.

1082
01:41:00,500 --> 01:41:02,550
Who was your atabey talking to?

1083
01:41:03,320 --> 01:41:05,550
When would he leave you?

1084
01:41:06,380 --> 01:41:08,580
Did he know anyone in our tribe?

1085
01:41:08,580 --> 01:41:10,580
You are lying!

1086
01:41:10,580 --> 01:41:12,580
My atabey wasn't a traitor!

1087
01:41:16,300 --> 01:41:17,610
Die!

1088
01:41:44,950 --> 01:41:46,580
Son.

1089
01:41:49,270 --> 01:41:50,520
Alps!

1090
01:41:51,520 --> 01:41:54,670
Take him to İnegöl.

1091
01:42:24,350 --> 01:42:27,780
Clear the way!

1092
01:42:27,780 --> 01:42:29,780
Hang on, sister!
Hang on!

1093
01:42:33,810 --> 01:42:36,180
Clear the way!
We have wounded!

1094
01:42:36,180 --> 01:42:38,180
Hang on, Selvi!

1095
01:42:38,180 --> 01:42:40,700
Come on! Alps!

1096
01:42:42,410 --> 01:42:45,520
Women, inform Ayşe Hatun!

1097
01:42:45,520 --> 01:42:48,470
She was trained by Mother Selcan.
No one is better than her.

1098
01:42:48,470 --> 01:42:50,900
Come on! Come on!

1099
01:42:50,900 --> 01:42:52,010
Hang on, Selvi!

1100
01:42:52,010 --> 01:42:54,240
Come on, sisters!

1101
01:42:54,240 --> 01:42:57,500
Slowly, slowly!
Hold it tight!

1102
01:42:57,500 --> 01:42:59,500
Slowly!

1103
01:43:00,670 --> 01:43:02,040
Malhun!

1104
01:43:06,270 --> 01:43:07,300
Alaca!

1105
01:43:07,300 --> 01:43:08,550
Take Malhun to her tent.

1106
01:43:08,550 --> 01:43:10,440
No! My Selvi is dying!

1107
01:43:10,440 --> 01:43:11,950
You can't do anything, Malhun!

1108
01:43:11,950 --> 01:43:13,950
No, Bala! No!

1109
01:43:14,500 --> 01:43:15,840
My Selvi is dying!

1110
01:43:15,840 --> 01:43:18,410
You can't help like this, come on!

1111
01:43:18,410 --> 01:43:20,410
-Selvi!
-Malhun!

1112
01:43:21,440 --> 01:43:23,120
Don't scare your children!

1113
01:43:23,380 --> 01:43:25,240
Let's tend your wound, Malhun.

1114
01:43:25,980 --> 01:43:27,700
Aunt Selvi!

1115
01:43:36,900 --> 01:43:38,010
Mother!

1116
01:43:38,380 --> 01:43:39,580
Mother!

1117
01:43:39,580 --> 01:43:41,580
What's happening, mother?

1118
01:43:42,500 --> 01:43:44,040
I'm fine, my daughter.

1119
01:43:44,040 --> 01:43:45,840
Aunt Selvi?

1120
01:43:45,840 --> 01:43:47,210
Selvi will be fine too.

1121
01:43:47,410 --> 01:43:49,720
Fatma. Children.
Your mother is fine.

1122
01:43:49,720 --> 01:43:51,720
She'll be better after
we tend her wound.

1123
01:43:53,520 --> 01:43:54,840
You are fine, right?

1124
01:43:54,840 --> 01:43:56,380
Don't worry, Orhan.

1125
01:43:56,380 --> 01:43:58,380
Be with your sister.

1126
01:44:02,150 --> 01:44:05,100
Inform Barkın Bey at once!

1127
01:44:06,580 --> 01:44:08,700
She won't die, right?
Mother Bala?

1128
01:44:08,700 --> 01:44:09,580
She won't die?

1129
01:44:09,580 --> 01:44:11,670
My mother and Aunt Selvi won't die!

1130
01:44:11,670 --> 01:44:14,350
No, my pretty girl.
No. No.

1131
01:44:14,350 --> 01:44:15,520
Don't be afraid.

1132
01:44:15,520 --> 01:44:17,520
Your mother is fine.
She'll be better.

1133
01:44:17,520 --> 01:44:19,840
Your aunt Selvi also be
fine.

1134
01:44:19,840 --> 01:44:22,380
Orhan. Take your siblings.

1135
01:44:22,380 --> 01:44:25,720
Pray. Pray.
Pray and they'll heal.

1136
01:44:25,720 --> 01:44:27,720
Who did this treachery, Mother Bala?

1137
01:44:28,180 --> 01:44:29,470
We'll find out, son.

1138
01:44:29,470 --> 01:44:30,380
We'll find out.

1139
01:44:30,380 --> 01:44:32,190
We'll find out when your
father comes.

1140
01:44:32,190 --> 01:44:33,010
Come on.

1141
01:44:33,010 --> 01:44:35,010
Come on, sister.

1142
01:44:35,120 --> 01:44:39,900
Mother! Mother! You, my sibling...
Are you alright?

1143
01:44:39,900 --> 01:44:41,900
We are, my dear.

1144
01:44:41,900 --> 01:44:43,670
We are.
Don't worry.

1145
01:44:43,840 --> 01:44:45,010
Don't worry.

1146
01:44:45,010 --> 01:44:47,010
Go to your siblings.
Come on.

1147
01:45:16,010 --> 01:45:17,780
You were right.

1148
01:45:18,750 --> 01:45:20,980
Osman is in great trouble.

1149
01:45:20,980 --> 01:45:25,150
The real game is just starting for
Osman, Commander Romanos.

1150
01:45:25,150 --> 01:45:29,240
With our plot, we'll take his life.

1151
01:45:30,150 --> 01:45:32,980
We'll provoke Ali Bey against
Turgut.

1152
01:45:34,700 --> 01:45:39,720
That shepherd will answer for all the
Roman blood he shed.

1153
01:45:41,070 --> 01:45:44,700
I'll rip his flesh out.

1154
01:45:45,610 --> 01:45:49,100
I don't want to wait any longer,
Commander Romanos.

1155
01:45:51,580 --> 01:45:53,840
There is just one thing that bothers me.

1156
01:45:57,500 --> 01:45:59,980
He learned that I came to Bhytinia.

1157
01:46:01,580 --> 01:46:03,670
And where my soldiers were.

1158
01:46:06,270 --> 01:46:07,810
How did he know that?

1159
01:46:10,870 --> 01:46:12,870
I need to solve this first.

1160
01:46:13,550 --> 01:46:15,920
What's in your mind?

1161
01:46:16,700 --> 01:46:17,780
Listen to me well.

1162
01:46:20,010 --> 01:46:22,810
İnegöl Castle

1163
01:46:35,900 --> 01:46:37,720
Kutan! Call the healer!

1164
01:46:37,720 --> 01:46:38,750
As you order, my bey.

1165
01:46:38,750 --> 01:46:40,750
Turgut!

1166
01:46:41,240 --> 01:46:43,410
Murderer of my atabey, Turgut!

1167
01:46:46,950 --> 01:46:48,410
You are a murderer!

1168
01:46:49,900 --> 01:46:52,640
You lived through all this but you
don't ask why.

1169
01:46:53,010 --> 01:46:55,640
You don't understand the scheme
because of your naivity.

1170
01:46:55,640 --> 01:46:57,320
You are still saying murderer.

1171
01:46:57,700 --> 01:46:59,670
You are a murderer!

1172
01:46:59,670 --> 01:47:01,270
Listen to me!

1173
01:47:01,670 --> 01:47:04,980
Many Turkish beys were destroyed
because of idiot sons!

1174
01:47:04,980 --> 01:47:08,210
But know that I won't hurt
Ali Bey because of you.

1175
01:47:09,070 --> 01:47:10,520
Son.

1176
01:47:11,150 --> 01:47:14,150
Come on! Where is this healer?

1177
01:47:19,750 --> 01:47:21,180
Murderer!

1178
01:47:22,100 --> 01:47:23,980
It's important for us.

1179
01:47:23,980 --> 01:47:25,870
Do your best.

1180
01:47:25,870 --> 01:47:26,900
Don't worry, my bey.

1181
01:47:26,900 --> 01:47:28,610
Murderer!

1182
01:47:33,470 --> 01:47:35,180
You'll live, Mustafa.

1183
01:47:35,920 --> 01:47:39,750
For the future of the Turks,
you will live.

1184
01:47:43,440 --> 01:47:44,470
Selvi...

1185
01:47:45,300 --> 01:47:46,580
Selvi...

1186
01:47:49,500 --> 01:47:51,240
Selvi...

1187
01:47:51,870 --> 01:47:53,010
Ayşe Hatun.

1188
01:47:54,810 --> 01:47:56,070
Selvi!

1189
01:48:00,470 --> 01:48:01,580
Ayşe.

1190
01:48:03,640 --> 01:48:04,610
Selvi.

1191
01:48:07,040 --> 01:48:08,780
You don't speak, I know.

1192
01:48:08,780 --> 01:48:10,780
But it's not like that.

1193
01:48:10,780 --> 01:48:13,320
Please tell me.
How is my sister?

1194
01:48:18,410 --> 01:48:24,780
After all this time, I would want you
to hear good words from you.

1195
01:48:25,700 --> 01:48:27,520
But it's not good, Malhun.

1196
01:48:29,240 --> 01:48:32,300
Don't say it.
Don't say that, Ayşe.

1197
01:48:32,300 --> 01:48:33,440
I'll see my sister.

1198
01:48:33,440 --> 01:48:36,520
Wait. Wait.
Your wounds!

1199
01:48:36,520 --> 01:48:38,040
Ayşe, I'll see my sister.

1200
01:48:38,120 --> 01:48:40,550
Malhun! What happened?

1201
01:48:41,210 --> 01:48:42,270
Are you alright?

1202
01:48:43,240 --> 01:48:44,750
How did this happen?

1203
01:48:44,750 --> 01:48:46,070
Osman!

1204
01:48:47,470 --> 01:48:49,300
She is fine, my bey.

1205
01:48:49,300 --> 01:48:50,810
I tended his wounds.

1206
01:48:50,810 --> 01:48:52,810
She'll be fine.

1207
01:48:54,870 --> 01:48:56,180
Get well soon.

1208
01:48:56,180 --> 01:48:58,180
I'll be back later.

1209
01:49:02,670 --> 01:49:06,550
Osman. My sister is severely wounded.

1210
01:49:06,550 --> 01:49:07,870
She is fighting death.

1211
01:49:08,410 --> 01:49:10,120
It hurts me to lay here.

1212
01:49:10,120 --> 01:49:13,040
After your wound heals,
we'll go.

1213
01:49:15,610 --> 01:49:16,700
Selvi.

1214
01:49:18,150 --> 01:49:21,980
Selvi is left to my from my father,
my uncle.

1215
01:49:22,980 --> 01:49:24,950
She is struggling, Osman.

1216
01:49:24,950 --> 01:49:26,300
My heart is burning.

1217
01:49:26,300 --> 01:49:27,700
Wait now.

1218
01:49:28,240 --> 01:49:29,500
Wait now.

1219
01:49:31,810 --> 01:49:32,670
Malhun.

1220
01:49:32,670 --> 01:49:33,700
Mother!

1221
01:49:34,320 --> 01:49:35,780
My children.

1222
01:49:35,780 --> 01:49:37,780
My children!

1223
01:49:42,550 --> 01:49:45,720
Look, I'm fine.
Don't be afraid.

1224
01:49:45,720 --> 01:49:47,720
She kept crying since
she saw you.

1225
01:49:48,720 --> 01:49:52,780
I told her that our mother is
strong, that she'll be fine.

1226
01:49:53,320 --> 01:49:55,520
Nothing happens to mothers, right, father?

1227
01:49:55,520 --> 01:49:57,520
Mothers are very strong.

1228
01:49:58,700 --> 01:50:04,120
I told you. If the children
pray for their mother...

1229
01:50:04,120 --> 01:50:07,810
nothing happens to their mother.

1230
01:50:10,240 --> 01:50:14,520
My beautiful girl should never
be afraid.

1231
01:50:14,920 --> 01:50:16,210
I'm fine.

1232
01:50:16,210 --> 01:50:18,210
My beautiful mother.
Alright, I won't.

1233
01:50:20,580 --> 01:50:24,500
She won't. She won't.
My daughter knows her mother.

1234
01:50:24,500 --> 01:50:26,500
Her mother is strong.

1235
01:50:27,040 --> 01:50:28,320
I know.

1236
01:50:28,320 --> 01:50:31,300
My mother and aunt Selvi are
healthy.

1237
01:50:33,640 --> 01:50:36,520
You didn't believe me when
you were crying, Fatma Hatun.

1238
01:50:38,270 --> 01:50:39,610
And mother...

1239
01:50:39,810 --> 01:50:41,810
with the sword my
father forged for me...

1240
01:50:41,810 --> 01:50:46,640
I'll make them regret doing
this to you and my aunt.

1241
01:51:10,300 --> 01:51:11,920
O' the healer!

1242
01:51:12,610 --> 01:51:14,070
O' the healer!

1243
01:51:14,670 --> 01:51:16,180
O' the healer!

1244
01:51:18,500 --> 01:51:20,010
My Allah!

1245
01:51:21,840 --> 01:51:24,500
Selvi! Thank Allah, sister!

1246
01:51:24,500 --> 01:51:26,500
Thank Allah!

1247
01:51:28,350 --> 01:51:30,210
Bala...

1248
01:51:33,300 --> 01:51:34,670
Water...

1249
01:51:38,520 --> 01:51:40,120
Thank Allah!

1250
01:51:55,180 --> 01:51:56,700
Bala!

1251
01:51:57,900 --> 01:51:59,780
My time is over.

1252
01:52:01,670 --> 01:52:03,320
But I have to say it...

1253
01:52:04,320 --> 01:52:06,410
I have to get your blessing.

1254
01:52:06,410 --> 01:52:08,410
What are you saying, Selvi?

1255
01:52:08,410 --> 01:52:10,410
You'll heal, inshallah.

1256
01:52:13,150 --> 01:52:15,580
Malhun. Is my sister alright?

1257
01:52:15,580 --> 01:52:19,070
She is. She is. She'll come too.
Don't worry.

1258
01:52:19,240 --> 01:52:21,180
Thank Allah.

1259
01:52:22,150 --> 01:52:24,150
There is no time, Bala.

1260
01:52:24,950 --> 01:52:26,240
Barkın...

1261
01:52:27,350 --> 01:52:30,700
Whatever Barkın did,
he did it for us.

1262
01:52:32,580 --> 01:52:34,640
He did it for our tribe, Bala.

1263
01:52:34,640 --> 01:52:36,640
For my father's legacy.

1264
01:52:37,750 --> 01:52:39,300
Not because he is evil.

1265
01:52:42,240 --> 01:52:43,350
Selvi.

1266
01:52:43,920 --> 01:52:45,210
What are you saying?

1267
01:52:45,900 --> 01:52:49,410
Barkın Bey? What are you trying
to say?

1268
01:52:49,410 --> 01:52:53,410
I told Barkın, Bala...

1269
01:52:55,410 --> 01:53:00,240
I told Barkın that Turgut Bey
was going to İnegöl.

1270
01:53:00,750 --> 01:53:05,550
Give me your blessing.
Give me your blessing.

1271
01:53:07,520 --> 01:53:09,980
It's yours, sister.
It's yours.

1272
01:53:11,870 --> 01:53:14,270
But what did Barkın Bey do?

1273
01:53:15,640 --> 01:53:16,810
Barkın...

1274
01:53:17,810 --> 01:53:19,980
Barkın loves Osman Bey...

1275
01:53:23,100 --> 01:53:25,520
Ahmet Bey was Barkın's friend.

1276
01:53:25,900 --> 01:53:27,700
They were close.

1277
01:53:28,900 --> 01:53:31,350
But he wasn't deceived by them.

1278
01:53:31,700 --> 01:53:34,210
He didn't turn his back on Osman Bey.

1279
01:53:36,440 --> 01:53:38,410
Barkın isn't evil, Bala.

1280
01:53:38,410 --> 01:53:39,870
Know this.

1281
01:53:39,870 --> 01:53:42,210
I won't forget, sister.
I won't forget.

1282
01:53:43,300 --> 01:53:45,300
Tell me fully.

1283
01:53:45,870 --> 01:53:48,100
What did Barkın Bey do, Selvi?

1284
01:53:54,380 --> 01:53:55,520
Selvi!

1285
01:53:56,950 --> 01:53:58,300
Selvi!

1286
01:53:58,300 --> 01:54:00,300
Sister.

1287
01:54:00,300 --> 01:54:02,300
My beautiful sister.

1288
01:54:17,670 --> 01:54:19,380
Hang on, brother.

1289
01:54:19,380 --> 01:54:23,070
I'll be over.
It'll be over.

1290
01:54:23,070 --> 01:54:25,870
May Allah not test anyone with this.

1291
01:54:55,870 --> 01:54:57,320
What happened, Osman Bey?

1292
01:54:57,670 --> 01:54:58,980
Selvi Hatun.

1293
01:55:02,520 --> 01:55:05,150
Give me your blessing, sister.

1294
01:55:08,180 --> 01:55:09,920
You have mine.

1295
01:55:10,640 --> 01:55:13,010
You were my sister for years.

1296
01:55:16,670 --> 01:55:18,520
I couldn't protect you.

1297
01:55:20,040 --> 01:55:22,270
You give me your blessing.

1298
01:55:29,720 --> 01:55:31,920
She is wounded.
Inside.

1299
01:55:32,900 --> 01:55:33,720
Selvi?

1300
01:55:52,500 --> 01:55:53,750
Barkın.

1301
01:55:55,440 --> 01:55:56,720
My bey.

1302
01:56:07,100 --> 01:56:08,870
Get out.

1303
01:56:13,750 --> 01:56:16,180
Get out!

1304
01:56:40,640 --> 01:56:42,580
Go to Ali Bey.

1305
01:56:44,920 --> 01:56:47,210
And say that Osman killed Mustafa.

1306
01:57:00,920 --> 01:57:02,010
Barkın.

1307
01:57:04,550 --> 01:57:05,980
Barkın.

1308
01:57:08,150 --> 01:57:09,870
Thank Allah you came in time.

1309
01:57:11,470 --> 01:57:13,070
I couldn't, Selvi.

1310
01:57:14,120 --> 01:57:15,440
I couldn't.

1311
01:57:17,170 --> 01:57:19,520
I couldn't protect you.

1312
01:58:04,650 --> 01:58:10,060
-I killed all the irregulars.
-So you didn't take any captives again?

1313
01:58:15,120 --> 01:58:16,820
I don't understand, Osman Bey.

1314
01:58:16,960 --> 01:58:19,090
All the ones you brought were
poisoned.

1315
01:58:19,200 --> 01:58:21,370
They died without answering
anything.

1316
01:58:21,500 --> 01:58:23,560
I know, Osman Bey.

1317
01:58:29,130 --> 01:58:32,150
He drank poison when he realized
he'll be a captive.

1318
01:58:32,340 --> 01:58:35,510
He died when I was trying to
interrogate him.

1319
01:58:41,400 --> 01:58:44,170
If there is something behind this...

1320
01:58:44,600 --> 01:58:47,190
then consider your life taken.

1321
01:58:47,310 --> 01:58:49,190
There is nothing behind it, Osman Bey.

1322
01:58:49,680 --> 01:58:52,420
It's just Sultan's order.

1323
01:58:53,260 --> 01:58:56,030
I'll tell him about your help.

1324
01:58:58,400 --> 01:59:00,080
Are they all dead?

1325
01:59:00,330 --> 01:59:02,470
If you ask the Mongols,
they are all dead.

1326
01:59:02,690 --> 01:59:04,750
Who else would I ask?

1327
01:59:05,120 --> 01:59:07,210
I have a Byzantine.

1328
01:59:07,420 --> 01:59:10,340
Then why aren't you bringing him
instead of a corpse?

1329
01:59:10,630 --> 01:59:13,430
Cebe works for coins.

1330
01:59:14,180 --> 01:59:16,700
The Byzantine will be
worth a lot of coins.

1331
01:59:22,620 --> 01:59:26,790
Who is his owner?
Did he speak?

1332
01:59:27,470 --> 01:59:32,550
Rom... Roma...
Romanos!

1333
01:59:34,920 --> 01:59:36,570
Romanos.

1334
01:59:37,060 --> 01:59:40,960
So, Romanos rules all
the irregulars, huh?

1335
01:59:45,470 --> 01:59:47,770
I need that man.

1336
01:59:54,500 --> 01:59:57,610
Why is it so important for you?

1337
01:59:59,010 --> 02:00:02,060
Mustafa Bey was murdered.

1338
02:00:02,660 --> 02:00:07,890
Those who attacked him are
collaborating with them, obviously.

1339
02:00:09,700 --> 02:00:13,230
If the importance
is high, so is the price.

1340
02:00:13,520 --> 02:00:17,480
When I get him, you will get paid.

1341
02:00:25,970 --> 02:00:29,710
However Osman Bey wants.

1342
02:00:34,590 --> 02:00:36,960
You'll stand up, right?

1343
02:00:37,770 --> 02:00:43,250
We will leave this dire tent together
and go back to our tent, right?

1344
02:00:44,460 --> 02:00:47,590
You will go to our tent without me.

1345
02:00:48,710 --> 02:00:58,490
Take good care of my tent.

1346
02:00:59,620 --> 02:01:02,650
Don't turn your back to them.

1347
02:01:03,140 --> 02:01:05,240
Hang on, my Selvi.

1348
02:01:07,670 --> 02:01:09,770
Please.

1349
02:01:11,320 --> 02:01:13,780
Don't leave me.

1350
02:01:15,510 --> 02:01:18,100
Don't leave me.

1351
02:01:28,210 --> 02:01:30,540
Barkın Bey doesn't look well.

1352
02:01:31,780 --> 02:01:34,860
This much anger is not good.

1353
02:01:35,380 --> 02:01:37,530
Not at all.

1354
02:01:37,940 --> 02:01:40,500
I hope he doesn't do anything bad.

1355
02:01:42,190 --> 02:01:44,460
It's not easy, Malhun.

1356
02:01:44,640 --> 02:01:46,460
Not easy at all.

1357
02:01:51,970 --> 02:01:53,410
Malhun.

1358
02:01:56,050 --> 02:02:00,630
You should talk to Selvi.

1359
02:02:01,230 --> 02:02:03,380
She's said some things but...

1360
02:02:03,630 --> 02:02:05,990
if they are what I've thought about...

1361
02:02:07,540 --> 02:02:10,650
What did she say?

1362
02:02:13,050 --> 02:02:14,660
If you leave...

1363
02:02:17,110 --> 02:02:19,000
I'll be sad.

1364
02:02:19,210 --> 02:02:20,890
Don't leave me.

1365
02:02:22,600 --> 02:02:26,920
I bear witness that there is
no deity but Allah..."

1366
02:02:28,160 --> 02:02:33,930
"and I bear witness that
Muhammad is the messenger of Allah."

1367
02:02:37,790 --> 02:02:40,840
Selvi.

1368
02:02:41,360 --> 02:02:44,590
Selvi? Don't leave me.

1369
02:02:45,160 --> 02:02:47,260
Don't leave me.

1370
02:02:47,510 --> 02:02:49,660
Don't leave me, Selvi!

1371
02:02:54,860 --> 02:02:56,470
Selvi.

1372
02:02:58,920 --> 02:03:00,430
Selvi.

1373
02:03:12,170 --> 02:03:13,470
Selvi.

1374
02:03:13,650 --> 02:03:16,000
Malhun.

1375
02:03:19,650 --> 02:03:21,070
Selvi.

1376
02:03:24,440 --> 02:03:27,280
I couldn't protect her...

1377
02:03:28,830 --> 02:03:31,830
I couldn't protect her...

1378
02:03:47,770 --> 02:03:52,830
When a calamity befalls them, we certainly
belong to Allah and to Him we shall certainly return.

1379
02:04:00,580 --> 02:04:06,390
O, who believe in Allah. Don't betray
Allah and Muhammad.

1380
02:04:06,785 --> 02:04:11,105
If you do, you betray everything that is
given to you to take care.

1381
02:04:12,120 --> 02:04:13,460
Sheikh...

1382
02:04:13,700 --> 02:04:18,200
What is told in this verse? (ayet)

1383
02:04:20,420 --> 02:04:25,120
Bismillâhirrahmânirrahîm.
(in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.)

1384
02:04:26,120 --> 02:04:28,520
Here they are.

1385
02:04:29,140 --> 02:04:33,720
What is given to us are these.

1386
02:04:35,220 --> 02:04:43,810
Quran is Allah's sunnah.

1387
02:04:44,070 --> 02:04:45,780
However...

1388
02:04:46,560 --> 02:04:50,440
smart Muslims never betray.

1389
02:04:51,810 --> 02:05:03,370
There are smart and believing Muslims but
they betray Allah's sunnah anyway.

1390
02:05:03,870 --> 02:05:10,310
However, they don't even
recognize what they are doing.

1391
02:05:10,880 --> 02:05:14,710
They think Allah's bans and orders are...

1392
02:05:14,910 --> 02:05:20,490
...for only the jahiliyyah
(days of ignorance, before Islam)

1393
02:05:20,590 --> 02:05:27,960
...like there is no jahiliyyah
in the time we are living in.

1394
02:05:29,950 --> 02:05:31,550
They are mistaken.

1395
02:05:31,890 --> 02:05:36,650
Devil approaches them sneakingly.

1396
02:05:36,780 --> 02:05:43,440
Devil says: "times have changed...

1397
02:05:43,440 --> 02:05:47,900
...Allah's words was for those
times back then....

1398
02:05:48,160 --> 02:05:53,980
...now everyone does what they do
for themselves.

1399
02:05:54,160 --> 02:06:00,790
We are not intrested in anyone's sins
or virtues" The devil says.

1400
02:06:01,020 --> 02:06:04,430
He says: "Not my business".

1401
02:06:05,130 --> 02:06:08,310
A Muslim who says "not my business"...

1402
02:06:08,470 --> 02:06:13,080
... will betray the entrustment of Allah.

1403
02:06:13,390 --> 02:06:19,540
If a Muslim shuts his eyes to sins...

1404
02:06:19,830 --> 02:06:22,160
...and let it happen...

1405
02:06:22,570 --> 02:06:26,190
...it means he betrays
the entrustment of Allah.

1406
02:06:26,320 --> 02:06:30,200
But my Sheik, Islam is a
religion of latitude, isn't it?

1407
02:06:31,760 --> 02:06:34,080
No, my shahzade.

1408
02:06:34,470 --> 02:06:36,750
It is not, my Orhan.

1409
02:06:37,710 --> 02:06:43,840
Islam allows favour and beauty.

1410
02:06:44,200 --> 02:06:49,870
Islam doesn't allow the evil,
what Allah made Haram (forbidden)

1411
02:06:50,130 --> 02:06:57,970
Islam doesn't allow corruption, theft,
alcohol, gambling, adultery...

1412
02:06:58,230 --> 02:07:06,800
...the perversion of Lut tribe,
leaving the prayers and deceitfulness.

1413
02:07:07,590 --> 02:07:13,570
The more you allow the evil,
the more your life extends.

1414
02:07:13,850 --> 02:07:17,550
Islam does not let the evil live on.

1415
02:07:17,860 --> 02:07:20,240
Islam fights against it.

1416
02:07:20,790 --> 02:07:30,010
Nobody is more merciful than Allah to allow
anything that Allah does not.

1417
02:07:30,510 --> 02:07:34,500
Allowing what Allah does not...

1418
02:07:35,040 --> 02:07:37,180
...is a great arrogance.

1419
02:07:37,940 --> 02:07:41,100
This is shirk.

1420
02:07:42,490 --> 02:07:48,610
A Muslim must be on the alert.

1421
02:07:50,830 --> 02:07:55,780
You shall always stand against the evil.

1422
02:07:56,050 --> 02:08:01,870
Do not allow the evil and haram.

1423
02:08:02,350 --> 02:08:07,040
A Muslim does not allow the evil.

1424
02:08:07,180 --> 02:08:08,850
He interferes.

1425
02:08:09,220 --> 02:08:15,760
Do not be one of those who say
"not my business". Never.

1426
02:08:16,020 --> 02:08:19,570
May Allah prevent us from becoming
one of those, my Sheik grandfather.

1427
02:08:20,710 --> 02:08:23,330
May our Lord let us stay in His path.

1428
02:08:24,580 --> 02:08:27,080
Amen, sons.

1429
02:08:28,330 --> 02:08:31,950
May our Lord let you stay in His path.

1430
02:08:32,210 --> 02:08:33,580
Amen.

1431
02:08:34,730 --> 02:08:35,960
Amen.

1432
02:09:00,000 --> 02:09:01,250
Tell me.

1433
02:09:01,700 --> 02:09:04,470
What news Barkın Bey sent to me?

1434
02:09:08,460 --> 02:09:10,700
I told you to tell me.

1435
02:09:10,880 --> 02:09:12,450
My Bey.

1436
02:09:13,010 --> 02:09:15,090
Your son, Mustafa...

1437
02:09:18,610 --> 02:09:25,720
Osman... his nephew... stabbed Mustafa.

1438
02:09:27,910 --> 02:09:30,630
What are you saying?

1439
02:09:30,920 --> 02:09:33,590
I told you to take care of my son.

1440
02:09:33,960 --> 02:09:37,760
Where were you while
Osman was doing all this?

1441
02:09:38,730 --> 02:09:40,980
Where was Barkın?

1442
02:09:46,360 --> 02:09:49,380
Is my son alive?

1443
02:09:49,660 --> 02:09:50,910
I don't know, my Bey.

1444
02:09:51,420 --> 02:09:53,450
They were taking him to İnegöl.

1445
02:10:00,420 --> 02:10:10,570
They killed my brother and
they stabbed my son.

1446
02:10:14,250 --> 02:10:20,010
I came here to support Osman...

1447
02:10:20,510 --> 02:10:25,830
he stabbed my back many times.

1448
02:10:30,400 --> 02:10:39,240
I swear that I will harm
his tent and İnegöl.

1449
02:10:47,840 --> 02:10:49,690
Go to the tent.

1450
02:10:50,180 --> 02:10:52,570
Send news to other tents.

1451
02:10:52,960 --> 02:10:56,640
Find everyone who is able to hold a sword.

1452
02:11:00,490 --> 02:11:09,050
From now on, we have no other
choice than war and revenge.

1453
02:11:10,640 --> 02:11:12,010
Ali Bey.

1454
02:11:15,170 --> 02:11:17,080
Bring your army.

1455
02:11:18,750 --> 02:11:20,510
Burn the tent.

1456
02:11:21,630 --> 02:11:24,980
However, you may not find
Osman Bey when you come.

1457
02:11:33,370 --> 02:11:35,430
What are you saying?

1458
02:11:35,750 --> 02:11:39,860
Osman is walking into a trap
that will end himself.

1459
02:11:56,770 --> 02:11:58,750
Romanos.

1460
02:12:03,580 --> 02:12:05,610
We met again.

1461
02:12:05,780 --> 02:12:09,540
I've told you we will meet again.

1462
02:12:15,020 --> 02:12:17,030
Don't worry.

1463
02:12:17,760 --> 02:12:20,660
We will settle accounts.

1464
02:12:24,360 --> 02:12:25,950
Thank you, Cebe.

1465
02:12:26,440 --> 02:12:28,590
You got Romanos.

1466
02:12:32,600 --> 02:12:35,520
- You did well.
- Yes, Osman Bey.

1467
02:12:49,960 --> 02:12:52,480
Osman!

1468
02:12:54,970 --> 02:12:57,290
You should have not come here.

1469
02:13:33,170 --> 02:13:39,360
A wolf never gives up tracing its hunt
even if it's in hell.

